1
00:02:02,718 --> 00:02:06,760
Demons spent eons trying to conquer death.

2
00:02:07,218 --> 00:02:11,093
But their greed to rule the universe
led to their downfall.

3
00:02:11,385 --> 00:02:12,677
Even in the Kali Yuga,

4
00:02:12,843 --> 00:02:15,635
mankind still seeks immortality.

5
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:18,010
Yet they cannot comprehend

6
00:02:18,510 --> 00:02:22,218
that God is both
the beginning and the end.

7
00:02:22,593 --> 00:02:26,385
Still, they search for a way
to conquer death.

8
00:02:27,093 --> 00:02:30,385
What power governs the universe today?

9
00:02:31,052 --> 00:02:32,093
And where does it dwell?

10
00:02:37,427 --> 00:02:40,802
Zulfi! Was this the place
where Abdali fought in 1757?

11
00:02:43,510 --> 00:02:46,593
Prabhakar's research papers
mention this very place.

12
00:02:50,968 --> 00:02:52,927
Tesla!

13
00:03:01,343 --> 00:03:02,968
Tesla! Give me your hand.

14
00:03:03,718 --> 00:03:04,343
Come on!

15
00:03:55,605 --> 00:03:57,730
Abdali!

16
00:04:06,093 --> 00:04:07,677
Come!

17
00:04:15,593 --> 00:04:17,843
Abdali!

18
00:04:40,010 --> 00:04:41,802
Come!

19
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,843
Come!

20
00:04:56,302 --> 00:05:01,357
Have you come, Abdali?

21
00:05:08,968 --> 00:05:12,177
Have you come, Abdali?

22
00:05:42,802 --> 00:05:46,177
Remember this, Afghan Sultan Abdali.

23
00:05:46,718 --> 00:05:50,010
We both have the same goal.

24
00:05:50,802 --> 00:05:53,801
To open the Nagabandha gate.

25
00:05:53,802 --> 00:05:56,510
To rule over this creation.

26
00:06:00,218 --> 00:06:06,510
For that to happen,
The keys to opening that gate,

27
00:06:09,385 --> 00:06:11,592
the Sacred Lotus,
and the Garuda mantras,

28
00:06:11,593 --> 00:06:13,676
must fall into our hands.

29
00:06:13,677 --> 00:06:16,177
Find them, wherever they may be.

30
00:06:19,718 --> 00:06:20,718
Go!

31
00:06:23,427 --> 00:06:24,885
Go!

32
00:09:04,968 --> 00:09:06,052
Dear students!

33
00:09:06,635 --> 00:09:07,760
Assemble here.

34
00:09:10,218 --> 00:09:11,343
Remember one thing.

35
00:09:11,677 --> 00:09:15,968
You would need a lifetime to find
even one of the artefacts shown here.

36
00:09:16,427 --> 00:09:19,468
Yet one man discovered them all.

37
00:09:20,010 --> 00:09:22,843
The longest-serving director
in Indian archaeology,

38
00:09:23,718 --> 00:09:30,218
a man capable of deciphering
any archaeological inscription,

39
00:09:30,427 --> 00:09:33,260
I present to you
the archaeological genius, Mr. Prabhakar.

40
00:09:42,885 --> 00:09:45,010
Welcome, sir. Please.

41
00:09:48,093 --> 00:09:50,927
- [all] Pleasure to meet you, sir!
- Thank you. Thank you!

42
00:09:51,427 --> 00:09:55,677
Sir, the world knows
about your achievements and legacy.

43
00:09:56,093 --> 00:09:57,510
But your failure…

44
00:10:02,385 --> 00:10:04,093
Sir? Sir!

45
00:10:10,593 --> 00:10:13,010
Some questions shape the future.

46
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:14,968
And some others…

47
00:10:16,385 --> 00:10:17,677
haunt the past.

48
00:10:18,093 --> 00:10:19,593
What exactly is it, sir?

49
00:10:23,427 --> 00:10:26,927
The Virata Purusha form
Vishnu assumed on Earth,

50
00:10:28,593 --> 00:10:32,177
a marvel before which
even the mighty Himalayas bowed.

51
00:10:35,093 --> 00:10:38,510
He who turned the infinite cosmos
into a lotus and bore it upon his navel…

52
00:10:40,218 --> 00:10:42,343
a temple dedicated to that Virata Purusha.

53
00:10:43,093 --> 00:10:44,593
The search for it

54
00:10:45,385 --> 00:10:50,177
consumed thirty years
of my life and experience.

55
00:10:51,635 --> 00:10:53,177
This defeat isn't mine alone.

56
00:10:54,302 --> 00:10:56,802
It left a bitter mark
on many throughout history.

57
00:10:57,177 --> 00:11:00,302
- So there's no path to it now, sir?
- There is.

58
00:11:02,385 --> 00:11:05,718
In 1757, Sultan Abdali
of Afghanistan and his minister

59
00:11:06,093 --> 00:11:11,635
supposedly wrote a book about
the temple attack and the path to it.

60
00:11:12,635 --> 00:11:14,218
This inscription claims so.

61
00:11:14,552 --> 00:11:17,593
That book is the only guide to the path.

62
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:20,510
So … where is that book, sir?

63
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:40,302
- Sir. Tesla here.
- Yes, Tesla.

64
00:11:40,427 --> 00:11:43,385
- I must speak to Mr. Prabhakar urgently.
- Wait a minute.

65
00:11:45,885 --> 00:11:48,552
Sir! Tesla is on the phone.

66
00:11:50,052 --> 00:11:51,052
He says it's urgent.

67
00:11:56,593 --> 00:11:57,802
- Sorry! Sorry!
- Hey!

68
00:11:58,677 --> 00:12:00,885
- [in Hindi] Watch where you're going!
- Please forgive me.

69
00:12:01,093 --> 00:12:02,468
- Where do these people come from?
- Sorry.

70
00:12:12,968 --> 00:12:14,843
Stop! Stop!
[in Hindi] Do you have a pass?

71
00:12:15,593 --> 00:12:18,718
- Sir!
- Security, let him in.

72
00:12:19,135 --> 00:12:21,677
- He's our guy.
- Okay, sir! Go!

73
00:12:31,593 --> 00:12:33,843
This summit
will greatly benefit the country.

74
00:12:33,968 --> 00:12:36,670
- Your support is vital for our nation.
- Mr. Murali Prasad!

75
00:12:38,635 --> 00:12:40,968
Prabhakar? Excuse me.

76
00:12:43,843 --> 00:12:44,802
Yes, Prabhakar.

77
00:12:45,677 --> 00:12:48,343
I need to meet the Prime Minister
immediately. It's an important matter.

78
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:51,177
Everything here is important.

79
00:12:51,677 --> 00:12:53,927
No one meets the Prime Minister casually.

80
00:12:54,843 --> 00:12:57,593
We have rules and protocols.

81
00:12:58,677 --> 00:13:01,093
Come to the office tomorrow morning.
We'll discuss it then.

82
00:13:01,218 --> 00:13:04,052
Sir, it's very important.

83
00:13:05,218 --> 00:13:06,092
Who is he?

84
00:13:06,093 --> 00:13:09,302
He's Tesla, an archaeology
research scholar.

85
00:13:09,510 --> 00:13:11,010
- Oh!
- Trust me.

86
00:13:11,468 --> 00:13:13,468
This is going to change India's future.

87
00:13:13,885 --> 00:13:15,968
This meeting
is also about Indians' future.

88
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:20,885
The inscriptions and relics
you discover won't change the future.

89
00:13:21,802 --> 00:13:24,552
But… policies will change India

90
00:13:24,968 --> 00:13:26,927
by creating big wealth.

91
00:13:27,218 --> 00:13:29,510
Sir, what you're talking about

92
00:13:29,635 --> 00:13:31,802
is the wealth
India may gain in the future.

93
00:13:32,468 --> 00:13:34,927
But what I'm talking about

94
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:39,010
is the immense wealth
already hidden in this country.

95
00:13:40,885 --> 00:13:44,052
Come on, Tesla!
Prabhakar, enjoy the evening.

96
00:13:44,885 --> 00:13:45,927
Sir, hear me out!

97
00:13:46,885 --> 00:13:48,218
It's about Nagabandham.

98
00:13:51,885 --> 00:13:53,218
What nonsense are you talking?

99
00:13:54,802 --> 00:13:56,302
Do you even know what you're saying?

100
00:13:57,135 --> 00:14:00,510
This isn't what you told me before!
You think this is a joke?

101
00:14:02,260 --> 00:14:04,635
People have only heard about Nagabandham.
No one has ever seen it.

102
00:14:05,385 --> 00:14:08,302
Our archaeology department
has researched it for years.

103
00:14:08,593 --> 00:14:09,968
We never found a single clue.

104
00:14:10,927 --> 00:14:12,177
But, I've got it, sir.

105
00:14:57,885 --> 00:14:58,760
Alright.

106
00:14:59,635 --> 00:15:01,302
You wait here, I'll come back.

107
00:15:05,843 --> 00:15:07,052
- Please!
- Of course!

108
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:09,093
Sir!

109
00:15:12,343 --> 00:15:13,218
Sure!

110
00:15:14,218 --> 00:15:15,052
Okay!

111
00:15:16,218 --> 00:15:18,759
The PM wants to see you
at his residence tomorrow at 8 AM.

112
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:20,260
- Okay, see you.
- Okay.

113
00:15:28,218 --> 00:15:30,593
- Sir, sir!
- Yes!

114
00:15:30,843 --> 00:15:34,427
[in Hindi] Sir! Please, sir!
Please buy a toy, sir.

115
00:15:34,677 --> 00:15:37,677
Please, sir!
Please buy a toy, sir.

116
00:15:37,843 --> 00:15:39,760
- Please, sir!
- How much?

117
00:15:40,302 --> 00:15:41,718
Give me whatever you can, sir.

118
00:15:44,260 --> 00:15:45,510
Brother, whose vehicle is this?

119
00:15:47,177 --> 00:15:49,677
This is India, sir. We'll change India.

120
00:15:54,593 --> 00:15:55,468
Robert, stop the car.

121
00:16:03,218 --> 00:16:04,760
- Bye, sir!
- Tesla!

122
00:16:05,218 --> 00:16:07,427
- Yes, sir.
- Don't overthink it.

123
00:16:07,843 --> 00:16:10,260
It's Riya's birthday today.
Let's meet for dinner.

124
00:16:10,677 --> 00:16:12,468
- Hmm.
- Okay, sir. I'll see you.

125
00:16:28,552 --> 00:16:29,427
Riya!

126
00:16:30,792 --> 00:16:31,375
Daddy!

127
00:16:32,635 --> 00:16:33,968
Come on my dear baby!

128
00:16:37,510 --> 00:16:40,510
- Happy Birthday, baby! I love you!
- Thank you, Daddy.

129
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:42,093
Where's my gift?

130
00:16:42,968 --> 00:16:46,009
- I must've forgotten it in the car.
- It's okay, give after some time.

131
00:16:46,010 --> 00:16:47,302
- Are you sure? Come!
- I'm sure.

132
00:16:47,552 --> 00:16:48,967
- Come!
- Mom and I've been waiting

133
00:16:48,968 --> 00:16:50,759
for you for so long.

134
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:52,343
- Tessie!
- I'm sorry, baby!

135
00:16:53,302 --> 00:16:54,384
Why are you so late?

136
00:16:54,385 --> 00:16:55,343
Ah… Father!

137
00:16:55,593 --> 00:16:58,093
- Yes, my son?
- I have to make a confession.

138
00:16:59,177 --> 00:16:59,722
Come!

139
00:17:00,260 --> 00:17:01,635
Riya, go to mom.

140
00:17:03,343 --> 00:17:04,093
Come baby!

141
00:17:07,343 --> 00:17:08,843
Praise the Lord, Father!

142
00:17:08,968 --> 00:17:12,260
I made a mistake
hiding the truth about Zulfikar.

143
00:17:12,427 --> 00:17:17,468
Show me how I can atone for my mistake…

144
00:17:25,593 --> 00:17:26,385
Tesla!

145
00:17:33,468 --> 00:17:35,968
Praise the Lord, my son.

146
00:18:09,135 --> 00:18:11,885
- You?
- Yes, I am…

147
00:18:13,052 --> 00:18:15,427
the father of all sins.

148
00:18:26,718 --> 00:18:28,343
You just confessed…

149
00:18:29,177 --> 00:18:30,052
My son!

150
00:18:31,196 --> 00:18:32,904
Shall I tell you how to atone?

151
00:18:37,677 --> 00:18:39,885
Who decides

152
00:18:40,677 --> 00:18:43,718
the winner and loser

153
00:18:45,218 --> 00:18:47,010
in this game we played?

154
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:49,718
It's me!

155
00:18:50,635 --> 00:18:52,093
You cheat! I'll kill you!

156
00:18:55,218 --> 00:18:56,092
Daddy!

157
00:18:56,093 --> 00:18:56,927
Let me go!

158
00:18:57,177 --> 00:18:58,218
Mommy.

159
00:19:15,968 --> 00:19:17,760
Tesla!

160
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:21,885
Mommy!

161
00:19:26,135 --> 00:19:27,427
Hey, Tesla!

162
00:19:27,677 --> 00:19:28,593
Where is the book?

163
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:30,802
- Tesla!
- Tell me! Tell me!

164
00:19:31,968 --> 00:19:33,343
Daddy!

165
00:19:36,885 --> 00:19:42,510
Your… your scheme for the Nagabandham…

166
00:19:43,552 --> 00:19:46,260
will never succeed in this lifetime!

167
00:19:49,010 --> 00:19:49,843
No!

168
00:19:50,635 --> 00:19:51,760
No! No!

169
00:19:56,052 --> 00:19:57,842
Tesla! Tesla!

170
00:19:57,843 --> 00:19:59,010
Daddy!

171
00:20:01,552 --> 00:20:04,593
- Uncle, please… Uncle, please. No!
- Riya!

172
00:20:04,718 --> 00:20:07,385
Please leave my dad alone!

173
00:20:08,218 --> 00:20:11,301
Uncle, please release my dad!

174
00:20:11,302 --> 00:20:14,010
- Uncle! Please, uncle!
- Shh!

175
00:20:17,135 --> 00:20:19,968
Cute… cute baby.

176
00:20:20,927 --> 00:20:22,218
Were you scared?

177
00:20:23,468 --> 00:20:25,927
You don't have to be
scared, sweetheart.

178
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:28,135
He should!

179
00:20:30,593 --> 00:20:33,592
Your dad stole my book

180
00:20:33,593 --> 00:20:35,052
and hid it somewhere.

181
00:20:35,968 --> 00:20:42,260
My mom told me
never to take what belongs to others.

182
00:20:42,635 --> 00:20:47,176
If you want, I'll give you
all the toys I have.

183
00:20:47,177 --> 00:20:49,343
No! I want that book!

184
00:20:49,677 --> 00:20:51,509
- Let's play a game.
- Uncle, No!

185
00:20:51,510 --> 00:20:52,593
Your daddy will give it to me then!

186
00:20:53,218 --> 00:20:55,093
- What do you want?
- Uncle…

187
00:20:55,552 --> 00:20:57,052
What exactly do you want?

188
00:20:57,968 --> 00:20:58,885
Ask him.

189
00:21:01,677 --> 00:21:03,468
What's that book, Tesla?

190
00:21:04,010 --> 00:21:05,343
What's that book, Tesla?

191
00:21:07,593 --> 00:21:10,843
She's asking you, isn't she? Tell her!

192
00:21:12,135 --> 00:21:15,802
No matter how many lifetimes you live,

193
00:21:16,343 --> 00:21:17,677
you will never get it!

194
00:21:19,093 --> 00:21:22,093
Don't do this uncle! Please uncle!

195
00:21:25,802 --> 00:21:26,635
No!

196
00:21:31,177 --> 00:21:32,843
Uncle, don't!

197
00:21:56,427 --> 00:21:57,802
Riya, come back!

198
00:22:00,135 --> 00:22:02,593
Riya, just stay here!

199
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:06,093
Mommy! Uncle, no!

200
00:22:06,343 --> 00:22:08,385
- No, no! No, Uncle! No!
- Riya, come back!

201
00:22:10,135 --> 00:22:12,427
No… uncle…

202
00:22:13,218 --> 00:22:15,677
Uncle! No!

203
00:22:16,385 --> 00:22:17,385
Mommy!

204
00:22:19,927 --> 00:22:23,552
I will do as you said.
Please let my mommy go…

205
00:22:26,677 --> 00:22:27,635
Mommy!

206
00:22:30,927 --> 00:22:33,260
That's exactly what I'm saying, baby.

207
00:22:33,635 --> 00:22:36,635
But your daddy isn't listening.
What can I do?

208
00:22:36,927 --> 00:22:39,010
Give me the book and I'll let you all go.

209
00:22:39,927 --> 00:22:41,385
Otherwise, your mommy…

210
00:22:45,010 --> 00:22:47,302
Daddy! Daddy!

211
00:22:48,552 --> 00:22:49,843
Where is the book, Daddy?

212
00:22:51,802 --> 00:22:52,968
- Daddy!
- Sorry!

213
00:22:56,802 --> 00:22:57,510
Daddy?

214
00:22:59,135 --> 00:23:01,593
Daddy? No…

215
00:23:05,135 --> 00:23:06,968
Daddy, wake up!

216
00:23:10,635 --> 00:23:12,884
Daddy! Mommy!

217
00:23:12,885 --> 00:23:14,218
Tesla!

218
00:23:19,677 --> 00:23:20,677
God…

219
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:24,177
God is watching everything.

220
00:23:27,177 --> 00:23:30,510
He will surely… punish you!

221
00:23:32,427 --> 00:23:33,510
Daddy!

222
00:23:37,635 --> 00:23:38,802
Daddy!

223
00:23:39,677 --> 00:23:41,135
Ali! No!

224
00:23:41,552 --> 00:23:43,218
No! Riya!

225
00:23:58,802 --> 00:24:00,259
- Mrs. Padmamma!
- Namaste, Priest.

226
00:24:00,260 --> 00:24:03,052
The goddess Manasa Devi
is the primordial mother of all serpents.

227
00:24:03,218 --> 00:24:06,177
To that divine mother, everything offered,
be it ritual or offering, is only milk.

228
00:24:06,677 --> 00:24:09,885
Performing the first abhishekam
to the goddess with the milk you bring

229
00:24:10,010 --> 00:24:12,177
is a tradition passed down
through generations.

230
00:24:12,593 --> 00:24:15,885
- So, where are your son and daughter?
- They're coming.

231
00:24:32,718 --> 00:24:34,385
There she is! Ms. Manasa!

232
00:24:45,635 --> 00:24:47,468
It looks like Lord Shiva himself

233
00:24:47,635 --> 00:24:50,802
is carrying his child,
Manasa Devi, in his arms.

234
00:25:20,802 --> 00:25:22,010
My precious!

235
00:25:23,677 --> 00:25:24,552
Be careful!

236
00:25:26,427 --> 00:25:27,385
What is this, brother-in-law?

237
00:25:27,552 --> 00:25:30,635
Did you carry your sister
so her feet wouldn't hurt?

238
00:26:22,468 --> 00:26:23,427
Scumbag!

239
00:26:24,052 --> 00:26:25,010
Mr. Priest!

240
00:26:26,093 --> 00:26:27,885
As the festival day is auspicious,

241
00:26:28,177 --> 00:26:33,260
we've finalized Manasa's marriage
to Raju, son of Narasimha of Nagulakota.

242
00:26:33,718 --> 00:26:35,177
Say something, sister.

243
00:26:36,343 --> 00:26:37,343
What was that?

244
00:26:38,552 --> 00:26:41,343
There's already a groom in the house.
How can you marry her off to an outsider?

245
00:26:41,635 --> 00:26:42,843
What about our honor?

246
00:26:45,427 --> 00:26:48,510
We've been hoping to make Manasa
our daughter-in-law.

247
00:26:48,718 --> 00:26:49,802
No, sister-in-law.

248
00:26:50,135 --> 00:26:53,176
Raju and Manasa
have loved each other since childhood.

249
00:26:53,177 --> 00:26:56,260
Your husband died owing debts,
and that's become a burden now.

250
00:26:56,635 --> 00:26:59,635
My husband lent you our boat
so you could repay that debt, didn't he?

251
00:27:00,510 --> 00:27:03,760
You made money from it, and now
you want to marry her off to him?

252
00:27:04,510 --> 00:27:05,510
How is that fair?

253
00:27:06,510 --> 00:27:09,634
Out of the goodness of my heart,
I even overlooked that debt

254
00:27:09,635 --> 00:27:11,885
and thought of making Manasa
my daughter-in-law.

255
00:27:12,010 --> 00:27:15,135
Is our Kinka not handsome enough?
Is he not worthy?

256
00:27:15,760 --> 00:27:17,468
Hey, why aren't you talking?

257
00:27:17,885 --> 00:27:21,177
Aunt! A marriage without love
is never a good marriage.

258
00:27:21,302 --> 00:27:25,093
- Hey!
- How dare you push my sister?

259
00:27:26,260 --> 00:27:27,302
Who is your aunt?

260
00:27:27,927 --> 00:27:30,467
We don't know where you were born,
or even where you came from.

261
00:27:30,468 --> 00:27:32,302
Who are you to interfere in our matters?

262
00:27:33,552 --> 00:27:34,968
- Mom, stop it!
- Hey!

263
00:27:35,510 --> 00:27:37,717
- What your mom said is true, isn't it?
- Gandhar Raju, stop!

264
00:27:37,718 --> 00:27:38,676
Hey!

265
00:27:38,677 --> 00:27:40,635
He is an orphan
who doesn't know his mother!

266
00:27:40,968 --> 00:27:43,093
- A son who doesn't know his father!
- Hey!

267
00:27:45,385 --> 00:27:48,009
The moment you insulted my brother,
my hand rose on its own!

268
00:27:48,010 --> 00:27:49,677
One more word…

269
00:27:52,010 --> 00:27:53,384
- Hey.
- Hey…

270
00:27:53,385 --> 00:27:54,802
and I'll slash your neck.

271
00:27:55,010 --> 00:27:56,176
- Hey!
- Hey!

272
00:27:56,177 --> 00:27:57,010
Nephew!

273
00:27:58,802 --> 00:28:00,593
- Hey, stop!
- Manasa.

274
00:28:01,802 --> 00:28:02,802
I'm talking to you.

275
00:28:05,010 --> 00:28:07,760
In the name of Goddess,
I swear to everyone,

276
00:28:08,593 --> 00:28:09,635
Rudra is my son!

277
00:28:10,677 --> 00:28:11,552
My life!

278
00:28:14,010 --> 00:28:15,677
If anyone lays a hand on him

279
00:28:16,302 --> 00:28:20,260
or says even a single word against him,
I'll sever all relationship with them.

280
00:28:22,302 --> 00:28:23,260
Hey, Manasa!

281
00:28:29,468 --> 00:28:32,593
The principle was repaid,
what about the interest?

282
00:28:48,677 --> 00:28:49,760
Who's your aunt?

283
00:28:49,968 --> 00:28:52,510
We don't know where you were born,
or even where you came from.

284
00:28:56,052 --> 00:28:56,885
Brother.

285
00:28:57,927 --> 00:29:00,218
Are you drinking to relive the past
and forget the present?

286
00:29:01,802 --> 00:29:02,718
I mean…

287
00:29:03,010 --> 00:29:06,843
You've been hiding away, barely eating,
ever since the incident at the fair.

288
00:29:07,927 --> 00:29:10,718
Your sister could barely open the box,
yet she came to feed you.

289
00:29:11,510 --> 00:29:14,218
Alright, done feeling sad?
Shall I feed you?

290
00:29:15,473 --> 00:29:16,306
Feed him.

291
00:29:18,802 --> 00:29:23,385
Who feels bad for people who only act
when there's something in it for them?

292
00:29:23,635 --> 00:29:26,885
- What's this, brother? Our mom trusts you.
- After you feed him, he'll forget it all.

293
00:29:27,218 --> 00:29:29,010
And you are my life.

294
00:29:29,427 --> 00:29:31,135
Really? What about me?

295
00:29:32,427 --> 00:29:35,218
- Hey, Manasa! What about me?
- Hey!

296
00:29:36,593 --> 00:29:39,802
Rudra, you shouldn't be
thinking about them right now.

297
00:29:40,177 --> 00:29:41,385
You should be thinking about our wedding.

298
00:29:43,052 --> 00:29:46,343
Everyone from the surrounding villages
should attend. It must be a grand affair.

299
00:29:47,260 --> 00:29:49,259
Even if no one attends the wedding,

300
00:29:49,260 --> 00:29:51,676
my brother being there is enough for me.

301
00:29:51,677 --> 00:29:52,843
Not even me?

302
00:29:54,802 --> 00:29:56,135
When I think about your aunt,

303
00:29:56,593 --> 00:29:58,802
I feel like she might try
to stop this wedding.

304
00:29:59,093 --> 00:30:02,135
As long as my brother is with me,
who dares to stop this wedding?

305
00:30:02,302 --> 00:30:04,552
God! Always going on about your brother!

306
00:30:04,802 --> 00:30:06,260
After marriage, instead of
you coming to my house,

307
00:30:06,427 --> 00:30:09,092
I feel like I'll come
live in your house instead.

308
00:30:09,093 --> 00:30:12,843
That's how it is!
I will stay where my heart is.

309
00:30:13,010 --> 00:30:15,842
- Alright then. It's inevitable.
- Brother, it's getting dark.

310
00:30:15,843 --> 00:30:18,010
Let's go home, Mom will be waiting.

311
00:30:18,802 --> 00:30:20,677
You go ahead, I'll come later.

312
00:30:20,968 --> 00:30:22,385
- Come!
- Come quickly, Rudra.

313
00:30:22,968 --> 00:30:25,760
We're leaving now.
Let's meet tomorrow in Srirangapuram.

314
00:30:26,760 --> 00:30:29,510
[chanting]

315
00:30:37,427 --> 00:30:40,468
Everything will be fine
going forward, Janardhan.

316
00:30:42,385 --> 00:30:43,760
What do you mean, fine?

317
00:30:46,177 --> 00:30:49,342
The humiliation I faced at the fair today
felt like my head being cut off.

318
00:30:49,343 --> 00:30:52,427
Ignoring everything I said,
you kept supporting your sister.

319
00:30:52,718 --> 00:30:53,552
What happened now?

320
00:30:53,968 --> 00:30:56,218
Your sister's actions
haven't changed you at all.

321
00:31:07,302 --> 00:31:08,802
Sister!

322
00:31:10,302 --> 00:31:14,718
Seeing you like this
it hurts me deeply.

323
00:31:15,135 --> 00:31:18,218
Even though his sister
Padmamma insulted you so much,

324
00:31:19,343 --> 00:31:21,177
brother-in-law didn't say a word.

325
00:31:21,468 --> 00:31:23,427
He won't! Why would he?

326
00:31:23,593 --> 00:31:25,218
He loves his sister, doesn't he?

327
00:31:26,802 --> 00:31:29,677
He didn't react at all
even when they insulted me so much.

328
00:31:32,677 --> 00:31:34,802
Hey, Rudra! Come here.

329
00:31:35,093 --> 00:31:37,760
- May you live a hundred years! Come!
- Come!

330
00:31:43,593 --> 00:31:44,510
Hey!

331
00:31:45,510 --> 00:31:46,968
Rudra is one of ours!

332
00:31:47,343 --> 00:31:49,218
Go away! Move!

333
00:31:49,802 --> 00:31:50,552
I said go.

334
00:31:58,052 --> 00:31:59,343
Why did you come here?

335
00:32:00,302 --> 00:32:04,385
Uncle, I'm not old enough
to say this to you.

336
00:32:05,427 --> 00:32:06,718
What happened today was wrong.

337
00:32:07,468 --> 00:32:08,843
No matter who is responsible,

338
00:32:09,802 --> 00:32:11,302
everyone was hurt by it.

339
00:32:11,802 --> 00:32:13,843
I came here so that
this pain doesn't turn into anger.

340
00:32:15,052 --> 00:32:18,635
Whether good or bad,
you are all bound by blood.

341
00:32:19,468 --> 00:32:22,302
My sister did that out of love for me.

342
00:32:22,885 --> 00:32:25,385
She has neither
anger nor hatred toward you.

343
00:32:26,343 --> 00:32:28,385
Even if the whole village
attends her wedding,

344
00:32:28,718 --> 00:32:29,635
you're her uncle.

345
00:32:30,260 --> 00:32:32,552
Nothing can replace you.

346
00:32:33,843 --> 00:32:36,760
If I am the only problem here,
I'll leave after her wedding.

347
00:32:38,343 --> 00:32:39,592
- Hey!
- Brother!

348
00:32:39,593 --> 00:32:41,427
- Hey, Kinka! Hey.
- Who are you, man?

349
00:32:41,843 --> 00:32:43,468
What difference does it make
whether you stay or leave?

350
00:32:44,260 --> 00:32:44,885
Hey!

351
00:32:47,677 --> 00:32:49,677
- Hey!
- Brother, stop.

352
00:32:50,052 --> 00:32:52,468
That disgraceful woman is not my aunt,

353
00:32:53,343 --> 00:32:55,552
and the other worthless woman
is not my sister-in-law!

354
00:33:10,552 --> 00:33:11,718
I'll endure it.

355
00:33:12,552 --> 00:33:15,135
Call me anything you want.
I'll endure it!

356
00:33:17,260 --> 00:33:19,802
If you speak lightly
because I came to compromise,

357
00:33:20,593 --> 00:33:21,885
I will behead you.

358
00:33:22,802 --> 00:33:23,635
Is that clear?

359
00:34:19,510 --> 00:34:22,385
[Lord Rama hymn chant]

360
00:34:31,968 --> 00:34:35,093
Dear, Parvathi, your Guru is coming.

361
00:34:55,635 --> 00:34:58,177
Saraswathi,
are the prayer arrangements ready?

362
00:34:58,427 --> 00:35:00,759
Your disciple,
who knows your every routine

363
00:35:00,760 --> 00:35:04,427
- has already completed the arrangements.-Namo Narayanaya.

364
00:35:05,552 --> 00:35:07,134
Please bless me, Guruji.

365
00:35:07,135 --> 00:35:08,218
May you live a long life!

366
00:35:09,802 --> 00:35:11,552
She is another disciple.

367
00:35:11,968 --> 00:35:13,342
Her name is Priyamani.

368
00:35:13,343 --> 00:35:15,552
Sent by Raja Ravi Varma.

369
00:35:15,718 --> 00:35:18,593
She has come here
to learn the Vedas from you.

370
00:35:19,177 --> 00:35:22,343
Among all things in creation,
the wisdom of the Vedas alone is eternal.

371
00:35:22,968 --> 00:35:24,802
Learning the Vedas is not merely useful,

372
00:35:25,593 --> 00:35:27,760
It is a blessing.
I will definitely teach you.

373
00:35:46,093 --> 00:35:47,343
What is in that box?

374
00:35:48,177 --> 00:35:50,802
The key to the sanctum doors
of Ranganatha Swamy temple.

375
00:35:51,635 --> 00:35:52,552
And that?

376
00:35:54,260 --> 00:35:55,217
The Kunchakola.

377
00:35:55,218 --> 00:35:58,177
It is used to open the main temple doors.

378
00:35:59,093 --> 00:36:00,635
So many questions on your first day?

379
00:36:01,260 --> 00:36:02,718
I'll explain eventually.

380
00:36:28,802 --> 00:36:29,635
Greetings, sir!

381
00:37:39,135 --> 00:37:40,968
Govinda Govinda!

382
00:37:47,093 --> 00:37:50,177
Govinda Govinda!

383
00:38:27,552 --> 00:38:28,802
May you live long!

384
00:38:29,677 --> 00:38:31,302
Om Namo Ranganathaya Namahā!

385
00:38:33,552 --> 00:38:36,177
Are the arrangements
for the Lord's festival going well?

386
00:38:36,427 --> 00:38:40,260
By the grace of sacred chants,

387
00:38:40,718 --> 00:38:42,218
everything is going in perfect order.

388
00:38:43,260 --> 00:38:46,052
Though our family has overseen
the temple for generations,

389
00:38:46,385 --> 00:38:48,135
its true responsibility rests with you.

390
00:38:49,177 --> 00:38:53,384
As long as the temple and its traditions
are under your care, we can rest easy.

391
00:38:53,385 --> 00:38:55,718
I bow to Lord Narayana!
That is our good fortune.

392
00:38:56,593 --> 00:38:58,885
As you said, this temple is extraordinary.

393
00:38:59,843 --> 00:39:02,510
It is ancient and immensely significant.

394
00:39:04,427 --> 00:39:08,843
It is our fortune to be entrusted
with conducting these celebrations.

395
00:39:09,343 --> 00:39:11,843
May it be auspicious.
I shall take my leave.

396
00:39:12,927 --> 00:39:15,177
Om Namo Narayanaya!

397
00:39:15,885 --> 00:39:16,760
Wait, Parvathi.

398
00:39:16,927 --> 00:39:20,092
Guruji, may I ask a small doubt?

399
00:39:20,093 --> 00:39:21,052
Go ahead, dear.

400
00:39:21,177 --> 00:39:24,177
Every day the deity is adorned
with different decorations, right?

401
00:39:24,802 --> 00:39:28,468
Even if it's priceless, why hold
a grand festival for a golden flower?

402
00:39:29,760 --> 00:39:32,759
Festivals are not about
form or splendor, my dear.

403
00:39:32,760 --> 00:39:33,884
There she goes again.

404
00:39:33,885 --> 00:39:35,802
They are dedicated to the divine essence.

405
00:39:36,677 --> 00:39:39,885
To keep society united
and free of divisions,

406
00:39:40,510 --> 00:39:43,718
the Creator established
festivals as a sacred bond.

407
00:39:44,385 --> 00:39:47,135
It is not a golden flower,
but the Sacred Lotus.

408
00:39:48,052 --> 00:39:52,260
Its power and significance
may sound like mere folklore to you.

409
00:39:52,802 --> 00:39:55,260
- Wait. Dear Parvathi.
- Guruji?

410
00:39:55,427 --> 00:39:58,885
Can you tell this girl, in simple words,

411
00:39:59,468 --> 00:40:02,010
what you found
in your research about this temple?

412
00:40:03,302 --> 00:40:05,218
In the mid-17th century,

413
00:40:05,427 --> 00:40:07,510
this Ranganatha Swamy temple
was destroyed by fire.

414
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:09,968
The then king, Ranga Martanda Varma

415
00:40:10,218 --> 00:40:13,468
went to the Himalayas
to rebuild the temple.

416
00:40:13,718 --> 00:40:16,301
There, while bringing Shaligram stones

417
00:40:16,302 --> 00:40:18,135
believed to be
the embodiment of Lord Vishnu

418
00:40:18,302 --> 00:40:22,718
a Naga Sadhu is said to have given him
this Sacred Lotus, as our history tells.

419
00:40:23,052 --> 00:40:28,052
That is why, every Kartika Purnima,
grand festivities are held here.

420
00:40:29,427 --> 00:40:32,093
Forgive me, Guruji.
I spoke out of ignorance.

421
00:40:33,510 --> 00:40:35,343
Young people don't ask from ignorance.

422
00:40:35,552 --> 00:40:37,010
They ask because they're curious.

423
00:40:38,052 --> 00:40:40,302
Our culture is praised by the whole world.

424
00:40:41,177 --> 00:40:43,843
Let us not diminish it. Do you understand?

425
00:40:45,468 --> 00:40:46,343
Let's go.

426
00:40:47,302 --> 00:40:49,385
Manasa, we've reached
your mother-in-law's village.

427
00:40:49,885 --> 00:40:50,718
Alright.

428
00:40:54,052 --> 00:40:54,718
Come, Rudra!

429
00:40:55,927 --> 00:40:57,718
- Brother-in-law!
- Are you sober now?

430
00:40:59,427 --> 00:41:00,468
Come!

431
00:41:02,718 --> 00:41:04,510
You look like a beautiful doll, dear.

432
00:41:05,677 --> 00:41:06,635
Your mother isn't with you?

433
00:41:06,843 --> 00:41:08,218
She's busy with the wedding preparations.

434
00:41:08,843 --> 00:41:10,468
Once you fulfill your vow to the Lord,

435
00:41:10,718 --> 00:41:12,593
you'll never have to point a weapon again.

436
00:41:12,829 --> 00:41:13,409
Come, brother.

437
00:41:13,718 --> 00:41:15,927
- You go ahead!
- Okay, you stay here. We'll be back.

438
00:41:16,843 --> 00:41:19,052
- Come on, dear.
- Hurry, the celebrations are beginning!

439
00:41:26,302 --> 00:41:31,343
♪ To Srinivasa, beloved of Lakshmi
Bestower of all auspiciousness ♪

440
00:41:31,677 --> 00:41:37,010
♪ Glory to Venkatesa
Lord of Venkatagiri ♪

441
00:41:37,177 --> 00:41:42,010
♪ Glory to Venkatesa ♪

442
00:41:42,135 --> 00:41:47,468
♪ Whose divine gaze enchants Lakshmi
And blesses all creation ♪

443
00:41:49,427 --> 00:41:53,552
♪ We bow before You
Again and again ♪

444
00:41:54,177 --> 00:41:58,634
♪ We bow before You
Again and again ♪

445
00:41:58,635 --> 00:42:03,552
♪ We bow before You, O Narayana
Endless salutations unto You ♪

446
00:42:07,885 --> 00:42:13,302
♪ We bow before You, O Narayana
Endless salutations unto You ♪

447
00:42:13,802 --> 00:42:18,342
♪ We bow before You, O Narayana
You are all things, in all places ♪

448
00:42:18,343 --> 00:42:23,427
♪ Remembering You brings prosperity
Meditating on You grants liberation ♪

449
00:42:23,552 --> 00:42:28,302
♪ Revered by the nine planets
Salutations to You, O Narayana ♪

450
00:42:28,427 --> 00:42:33,052
♪ Destroyer of demons
Hear our prayer ♪

451
00:42:33,260 --> 00:42:37,343
♪ Protect us and watch over us ♪

452
00:42:37,510 --> 00:42:42,301
♪ Dweller of the sacred Vamana shrine
O Srinivasa, guardian of the Kali Yuga ♪

453
00:42:42,302 --> 00:42:47,260
♪ We take refuge in You
O Lord of Vaikunta ♪

454
00:42:49,593 --> 00:42:54,467
♪ Salutations to Padmanabha
Salutations to the soul of all existence ♪

455
00:42:54,468 --> 00:42:56,967
♪ Salutations to the One
Worshipped by Lord Shiva Himself ♪

456
00:42:56,968 --> 00:42:59,384
♪ We worship You with all our hearts ♪

457
00:42:59,385 --> 00:43:04,218
♪ Salutations to Padmanabha
Salutations to the soul of all existence ♪

458
00:43:04,385 --> 00:43:06,802
♪ Salutations to the One
Worshipped by Lord Shiva Himself ♪

459
00:43:06,968 --> 00:43:09,427
♪ We worship You with all our hearts ♪

460
00:43:29,552 --> 00:43:33,635
♪ The gates of Vaikunta have opened ♪

461
00:43:34,427 --> 00:43:36,885
♪ The gates of Vaikunta have opened ♪

462
00:43:39,218 --> 00:43:43,885
♪ The gates of Vaikunta have opened
The sacred Uttarayana season has arrived ♪

463
00:43:44,093 --> 00:43:48,885
♪ The chanting of the Ashtakshari mantra
Bestows long life and prosperity ♪

464
00:43:49,010 --> 00:43:53,802
♪ Relieve the suffering
And hardships of the poor ♪

465
00:43:53,927 --> 00:43:58,593
♪ Free them from the bondage
Of their desires ♪

466
00:43:58,843 --> 00:44:03,759
♪ Strike down all calamity
Like a divine weapon ♪

467
00:44:03,760 --> 00:44:08,051
♪ O Lord of Lords
Shower Your mercy upon us ♪

468
00:44:08,052 --> 00:44:12,842
♪ Dweller of the sacred Vamana shrine
O Srinivasa, guardian of the Kali Yuga ♪

469
00:44:12,843 --> 00:44:18,010
♪ We take refuge in You
O Lord of Vaikunta ♪

470
00:44:20,385 --> 00:44:25,217
♪ Salutations to Padmanabha
Salutations to the soul of all existence ♪

471
00:44:25,218 --> 00:44:27,551
♪ Salutations to the One
Worshipped by Lord Shiva Himself ♪

472
00:44:27,552 --> 00:44:29,885
♪ We worship You with all our hearts ♪

473
00:44:30,010 --> 00:44:34,718
♪ Salutations to Padmanabha
Salutations to the soul of all existence ♪

474
00:44:34,843 --> 00:44:37,343
♪ Salutations to the One
Worshipped by Lord Shiva Himself ♪

475
00:44:37,468 --> 00:44:40,260
♪ We worship You with all our hearts ♪

476
00:44:59,927 --> 00:45:06,468
♪ Salutations to You, O Narayana ♪

477
00:45:07,260 --> 00:45:13,135
♪ Glory to You, O Hari ♪

478
00:45:14,218 --> 00:45:19,010
♪ O Narayana ♪

479
00:45:19,510 --> 00:45:24,968
♪ Glory to You, O Hari ♪

480
00:48:48,635 --> 00:48:49,635
Robert!

481
00:50:45,677 --> 00:50:46,843
Sir, it's too risky.

482
00:50:47,677 --> 00:50:50,010
We can't go back. Keep going!

483
00:51:16,718 --> 00:51:18,343
- I've lost control.
- Take control!

484
00:51:18,510 --> 00:51:19,760
Hold on tight, sir.

485
00:51:19,927 --> 00:51:20,927
Hold on!

486
00:51:35,093 --> 00:51:36,177
I'm talking to you.

487
00:51:36,302 --> 00:51:38,718
I told you I don't want to go.
How many times must I say it?

488
00:51:38,843 --> 00:51:40,343
Raja doesn't listen
no matter what I say, brother.

489
00:51:40,677 --> 00:51:45,052
I went fishing for a small fish
and ended up with a whale.

490
00:51:45,218 --> 00:51:46,427
I told you to send them away.

491
00:51:46,927 --> 00:51:49,718
Hey Rudra, come on!

492
00:51:49,968 --> 00:51:53,135
- You're right on time.
- What's wrong, brother-in-law?

493
00:51:53,843 --> 00:51:55,467
No matter what I say,

494
00:51:55,468 --> 00:51:57,260
Gandhar Raju insists
I take them to Bhairavakona.

495
00:51:57,802 --> 00:51:59,968
We know well enough,
no one goes there and comes back.

496
00:52:00,302 --> 00:52:01,927
Some guy Shera
from Srirangapuram is here

497
00:52:02,052 --> 00:52:04,093
and he wants us
to take them there in our boat.

498
00:52:04,343 --> 00:52:07,093
They didn't come here asking for help,

499
00:52:07,718 --> 00:52:10,677
or demanding servitude.

500
00:52:10,843 --> 00:52:12,509
I brought these city folks here

501
00:52:12,510 --> 00:52:16,135
since they offered us some good money.

502
00:52:18,927 --> 00:52:21,843
Rudra, you can clear your debts.

503
00:52:22,135 --> 00:52:26,052
Your sister's wedding
can take place without a hitch.

504
00:52:38,343 --> 00:52:41,593
If money solves everything,
I'll take them.

505
00:52:42,968 --> 00:52:45,427
We caught the big fish.

506
00:52:45,968 --> 00:52:48,385
What are you saying?
Don't do this, Rudra!

507
00:52:49,010 --> 00:52:51,385
I don't know what Gandhara Raju
has in mind, brother-in-law.

508
00:52:51,885 --> 00:52:55,093
But all that's on my mind
is my sister's wedding.

509
00:53:30,635 --> 00:53:31,552
Hey!

510
00:53:31,802 --> 00:53:33,760
Why are you going to Bhairavakona?

511
00:53:36,385 --> 00:53:38,510
I'm asking you. What are we after?

512
00:53:40,385 --> 00:53:41,385
Well…

513
00:53:43,343 --> 00:53:46,843
that thing is as valuable
as it is dangerous.

514
00:53:47,718 --> 00:53:50,385
It's called… Sacred Lotus.

515
00:53:50,552 --> 00:53:51,760
What, a lotus?

516
00:53:53,427 --> 00:53:55,176
Someone like you wouldn't know its worth.

517
00:53:55,177 --> 00:53:58,968
Worth? Who risks their life
over a flower and some money?

518
00:53:59,302 --> 00:54:00,302
Come on, man.

519
00:54:01,093 --> 00:54:03,052
Hey, what's with your arrogance?

520
00:54:05,677 --> 00:54:07,093
I was born with it.

521
00:54:55,718 --> 00:54:56,843
What in the hell is this?

522
00:54:58,843 --> 00:55:00,843
Bhairavakona.

523
00:55:02,468 --> 00:55:03,843
Bhairavakona!

524
00:55:10,302 --> 00:55:12,093
Hey, keep moving forward.

525
00:55:12,802 --> 00:55:15,468
Anyone who goes ahead
never comes back.

526
00:55:18,218 --> 00:55:20,093
Why? Are you scared?

527
00:56:01,302 --> 00:56:03,468
- Let's move.
- Let's move.

528
00:56:26,510 --> 00:56:28,218
- Hey!
- They…

529
00:56:28,427 --> 00:56:30,635
are children of the forest, not beasts.

530
00:56:30,885 --> 00:56:31,802
- Leave.
- Hey!

531
00:57:00,093 --> 00:57:00,927
Hey!

532
00:57:18,052 --> 00:57:18,968
Hey!

533
00:57:31,885 --> 00:57:34,302
Anyone who stands in my way,

534
00:57:34,635 --> 00:57:36,760
I'll kill them. Even if it's you.

535
00:57:59,135 --> 00:58:00,093
Don't be afraid.

536
00:58:00,510 --> 00:58:02,802
Nothing will happen. It's only a sedative.

537
00:58:03,802 --> 00:58:05,343
What do you want anyway?

538
00:58:06,052 --> 00:58:07,010
The Sacred Lotus?

539
00:58:07,927 --> 00:58:10,760
No matter how hard it is, I'll bring it.

540
00:58:11,302 --> 00:58:12,010
What do you say?

541
00:58:36,635 --> 00:58:37,552
Let's hold it!

542
00:58:42,093 --> 00:58:43,760
Th-- The Sacred Lotus.

543
00:58:44,468 --> 00:58:45,635
It's aboard that flight.

544
00:58:49,468 --> 00:58:50,343
Will you go?

545
00:58:51,385 --> 00:58:52,552
You gave your word.

546
00:58:54,218 --> 00:58:55,302
Now, you go.

547
01:00:49,135 --> 01:00:50,552
Hey!

548
01:00:50,843 --> 01:00:52,177
Hey! Jump!

549
01:03:48,260 --> 01:03:50,135
Wake up! Wake up.

550
01:03:51,427 --> 01:03:53,760
- Brother. Please come here.
- Yes, dear.

551
01:03:54,218 --> 01:03:55,302
Please lend me a hand.

552
01:03:56,968 --> 01:03:59,510
- Hey, he's our Rudhra!
- Come on, help him.

553
01:05:37,552 --> 01:05:38,843
Can I ask you something?

554
01:05:42,385 --> 01:05:45,510
I saw you once
at the Srirangapuram festivities.

555
01:05:50,177 --> 01:05:52,552
You remembered me rather well,
for having seen me only once.

556
01:05:52,718 --> 01:05:56,510
How could I ever forget
the moment my life truly began?

557
01:06:03,177 --> 01:06:05,302
Did I say something wrong?

558
01:06:07,677 --> 01:06:08,510
No.

559
01:06:13,552 --> 01:06:14,677
Abdali!

560
01:06:14,968 --> 01:06:16,552
It was within reach,

561
01:06:16,927 --> 01:06:18,593
and then it slipped away, Bhairagi.

562
01:06:18,760 --> 01:06:22,260
It reached exactly
where it was meant to, Abdali.

563
01:06:22,802 --> 01:06:24,927
Such is the power of Time.

564
01:06:25,260 --> 01:06:27,927
Just as Time brought you to me,

565
01:06:28,302 --> 01:06:33,093
that Sacred Lotus
would have reached its destined place too.

566
01:06:33,927 --> 01:06:38,010
Many soldiers
must fall before a war is won.

567
01:06:38,552 --> 01:06:44,676
Then to obtain the Sacred Lotus
that rules the universe,

568
01:06:44,677 --> 01:06:46,593
how many more heads must roll?

569
01:06:47,427 --> 01:06:49,093
I'll be back, Bhairagi.

570
01:06:49,927 --> 01:06:51,135
Not alone.

571
01:06:52,260 --> 01:06:53,843
Along with the Sacred Lotus.

572
01:06:55,802 --> 01:06:57,093
Abdali!

573
01:06:57,927 --> 01:07:00,385
On the next full moon,

574
01:07:01,093 --> 01:07:04,592
the Sacred Lotus
will reach its peak power.

575
01:07:04,593 --> 01:07:09,968
Its energy will free me
from this Tree of Time.

576
01:07:10,093 --> 01:07:11,551
Remember!

577
01:07:11,552 --> 01:07:13,885
This is my last chance!

578
01:07:28,010 --> 01:07:29,093
She…

579
01:07:29,593 --> 01:07:33,552
She and Shera have been missing
since the night of the Brahmotsavam.

580
01:07:33,885 --> 01:07:36,010
Do you know why I really came here?

581
01:07:41,427 --> 01:07:45,177
Why is he frozen in place instead of
telling us how the Sacred Lotus was lost?

582
01:07:45,593 --> 01:07:49,468
Mr. Achyutachari, what is all this?
Why won't you say anything?

583
01:07:50,343 --> 01:07:53,427
What can he say?
What is there to say?

584
01:07:53,927 --> 01:07:56,177
He can neither evade responsibility,
not escape from here.

585
01:07:56,427 --> 01:07:59,302
Just as he's been swallowing
the Lord's offerings every day,

586
01:07:59,468 --> 01:08:02,385
he may well have stolen
the Sacred Lotus too.

587
01:08:02,552 --> 01:08:03,635
Sriranga!

588
01:08:08,343 --> 01:08:11,427
What are you all even saying?

589
01:08:12,677 --> 01:08:16,010
It is not right to suspect a man

590
01:08:16,718 --> 01:08:21,093
who has devoted his entire life
to this temple of being a thief.

591
01:08:21,552 --> 01:08:26,177
Mr. Sarathi, humiliating him like this
without knowing the truth is not right.

592
01:08:26,677 --> 01:08:29,468
Ma'am, it's not him
who's being humiliated.

593
01:08:29,718 --> 01:08:30,760
It is the temple's legacy.

594
01:08:31,052 --> 01:08:33,802
He has dishonored a heritage
preserved for generations.

595
01:08:34,093 --> 01:08:35,552
Why are you silent, Mr. Varma?

596
01:08:38,802 --> 01:08:42,593
Mr. Achyuta, what is all this?
Why won't you say anything?

597
01:08:45,302 --> 01:08:49,718
If it is obvious that he did it,
why would we care about his opinion?

598
01:08:49,927 --> 01:08:51,510
- Throw him out.
- Huh?

599
01:08:51,760 --> 01:08:53,343
- Get out!
- Dear.

600
01:08:54,218 --> 01:08:55,760
- What are you doing?
- [all] Get him out. Now!

601
01:08:55,927 --> 01:08:58,593
- Stop it!
- [all] Get lost!

602
01:09:01,052 --> 01:09:03,177
It is not for you
to decide right from wrong.

603
01:09:03,427 --> 01:09:04,343
Only God can.

604
01:09:06,135 --> 01:09:10,760
He says the Lord's feet are his home,
the Lord's service is his breath.

605
01:09:11,135 --> 01:09:16,302
He tends to the deity in the sanctum
like a child in its mother's womb.

606
01:09:17,385 --> 01:09:18,927
Why would he ever commit such a sin?

607
01:09:21,093 --> 01:09:24,010
If you all truly believe he did this,

608
01:09:24,718 --> 01:09:26,427
I will prove that

609
01:09:27,427 --> 01:09:30,802
you are wrong to suspect him,
and wrong to shame him!

610
01:09:32,385 --> 01:09:34,552
Wherever the Sacred Lotus may be…

611
01:09:35,177 --> 01:09:36,427
I will bring it back.

612
01:09:39,593 --> 01:09:41,510
The reason I was lying there, wounded…

613
01:09:42,718 --> 01:09:44,052
was because of the Sacred Lotus.

614
01:09:45,010 --> 01:09:48,677
- What? You saw the Sacred Lotus?
- Yeah.

615
01:09:48,968 --> 01:09:51,802
Where did you see it? Where is it now?

616
01:09:53,718 --> 01:09:55,010
- That…
- Rudra!

617
01:09:55,218 --> 01:09:56,677
- Brother. Brother.
- Rudra!

618
01:09:56,843 --> 01:09:58,052
- Brother-in-law!
- Mom!

619
01:09:58,260 --> 01:09:59,302
Rudra!

620
01:09:59,968 --> 01:10:02,635
Why did you go to Bhairavakona? Huh?

621
01:10:03,260 --> 01:10:04,385
What is this, brother?

622
01:10:04,802 --> 01:10:07,135
Why would you risk your life
for my wedding?

623
01:10:07,593 --> 01:10:09,510
What would happen to us
if anything happened to you?

624
01:10:09,677 --> 01:10:11,760
How did you stay away from me
for so many days?

625
01:10:11,968 --> 01:10:13,135
- Tell me.
- Hey, Manasa!

626
01:10:13,802 --> 01:10:15,510
Are you trying to put him back to sleep?

627
01:10:16,635 --> 01:10:19,010
I kept telling him, Aunt.
But would he listen to me?

628
01:10:20,552 --> 01:10:23,427
He risked his life believing
Gandhara Raja's deceptive words.

629
01:10:24,302 --> 01:10:28,427
If this girl hadn't arrived in time,
we would've lost our Rudra.

630
01:10:33,510 --> 01:10:35,635
You didn't save just one life, dear.

631
01:10:36,218 --> 01:10:37,343
You saved three.

632
01:10:38,593 --> 01:10:40,468
Not three. Four.

633
01:10:41,760 --> 01:10:42,635
Alright.

634
01:10:43,260 --> 01:10:44,593
What do you say, brother-in-law?

635
01:10:47,052 --> 01:10:49,052
- What is your name, dear?
- Parvathi.

636
01:10:50,927 --> 01:10:53,218
From now on, you are one of our family.

637
01:10:54,885 --> 01:10:57,468
Manasa's wedding is in two days.

638
01:10:58,343 --> 01:10:59,843
You must come.

639
01:11:09,135 --> 01:11:13,927
♪ I'll give you stallions to ride
And a kingdom to rule ♪

640
01:11:14,218 --> 01:11:19,010
♪ I'll give you stallions to ride
And a kingdom to rule ♪

641
01:11:19,177 --> 01:11:28,885
♪ Come, O bridegroom
Ascend the sacred dais ♪

642
01:11:29,302 --> 01:11:35,135
♪ Come, O bridegroom
Ascend the sacred dais ♪

643
01:12:03,302 --> 01:12:06,801
♪ Let the stars whirl and shine
Hoy! Hoy! ♪

644
01:12:06,802 --> 01:12:10,052
♪ Let us raise festoons afar
Hoy! Hoy! ♪

645
01:12:10,177 --> 01:12:13,468
♪ Slaughter the finest rams
Hoy! Hoy! ♪

646
01:12:13,635 --> 01:12:16,884
♪ Cook the choicest goats
Hoy! Hoy! ♪

647
01:12:16,885 --> 01:12:20,093
♪ The village has woven
A silken bridal saree ♪

648
01:12:20,218 --> 01:12:23,510
♪ The goddess herself has sent
Her blessings upon you ♪

649
01:12:23,718 --> 01:12:27,052
♪ The heavens descend
To raise these wedding canopies ♪

650
01:12:27,177 --> 01:12:30,302
♪ Mother Earth herself
Has laid this sacred altar ♪

651
01:12:30,427 --> 01:12:34,092
♪ Kith and kin gather
To shower blessings upon you ♪

652
01:12:34,093 --> 01:12:37,218
♪ Let this wedding
Be celebrated grandly ♪

653
01:12:39,052 --> 01:12:42,592
♪ Blow the sacred horn
Proclaim it aloud ♪

654
01:12:42,593 --> 01:12:45,926
♪ Lift the bridal palanquin
Hailo Hailessa ♪

655
01:12:45,927 --> 01:12:49,426
♪ Bring forth the feast
From river and field ♪

656
01:12:49,427 --> 01:12:52,802
♪ Let joy whirl around
Hailo Hailessa ♪

657
01:13:54,552 --> 01:13:58,884
♪ When he clasps my fingers
My anklets softly chime ♪

658
01:13:58,885 --> 01:14:03,052
♪ My cheeks bloom red
Like the Moduga flower ♪

659
01:14:03,177 --> 01:14:06,551
♪ Pearl-like grains adorn
Her radiant face ♪

660
01:14:06,552 --> 01:14:10,009
♪ The groom shines like a gem
Draped in silken grace ♪

661
01:14:10,010 --> 01:14:16,510
♪ The daughter raised with love
Leaves her mother behind today ♪

662
01:14:16,843 --> 01:14:21,134
♪ When he clasps my fingers
My anklets softly chime ♪

663
01:14:21,135 --> 01:14:25,718
♪ My cheeks bloom red
Like the Moduga flower ♪

664
01:14:27,385 --> 01:14:30,759
♪ Your love overflows
Like an endless river ♪

665
01:14:30,760 --> 01:14:33,802
♪ Protect us always
O noble lord ♪

666
01:14:34,218 --> 01:14:37,426
♪ Like Ganga and Gowri
We place our faith in you ♪

667
01:14:37,427 --> 01:14:40,842
♪ She crosses her village
To belong to another home ♪

668
01:14:40,843 --> 01:14:44,217
♪ All our people pray
She stays blessed with you ♪

669
01:14:44,218 --> 01:14:47,759
♪ Even if life demands sacrifice
She remains my soul ♪

670
01:14:47,760 --> 01:14:50,926
♪ I swear upon
The blood within me ♪

671
01:14:50,927 --> 01:14:54,592
♪ Wherever I may be
I shall guard her in my heart ♪

672
01:14:54,593 --> 01:14:58,343
♪ I shall remain beside her
Like a shadow ♪

673
01:14:59,718 --> 01:15:03,176
♪ Blow the sacred horn
Proclaim it aloud ♪

674
01:15:03,177 --> 01:15:06,302
♪ Lift the bridal palanquin
Hailo Hailessa ♪

675
01:15:06,510 --> 01:15:10,009
♪ Bring forth the feast
From river and field ♪

676
01:15:10,010 --> 01:15:13,343
♪ Let joy whirl around
Hailo Hailessa ♪

677
01:15:59,885 --> 01:16:00,885
Raja!

678
01:16:03,343 --> 01:16:04,343
Raja!

679
01:16:24,677 --> 01:16:25,843
Dear!

680
01:16:32,177 --> 01:16:33,218
Dear!

681
01:16:36,718 --> 01:16:38,427
Raju! Raju!

682
01:16:41,302 --> 01:16:43,802
- Raja…
- Oh God!

683
01:16:48,802 --> 01:16:50,093
Oh no!

684
01:17:07,177 --> 01:17:08,427
Suvarna!

685
01:17:08,802 --> 01:17:12,135
You really wanted to get married, huh?

686
01:17:12,510 --> 01:17:14,426
You were meant to be in my bed.

687
01:17:14,427 --> 01:17:16,135
If you insist on being with him…

688
01:17:16,593 --> 01:17:19,385
do you think I'll let you? Come!

689
01:17:20,218 --> 01:17:22,802
You're making a mistake! Let her go!

690
01:17:23,885 --> 01:17:24,760
Sister!

691
01:17:25,135 --> 01:17:27,010
Hey! Let her go! I'm talking to yo--

692
01:17:29,635 --> 01:17:31,593
- Hey, he's your father!
- Hey!

693
01:17:33,010 --> 01:17:35,343
You watched while I was humiliated!

694
01:17:35,927 --> 01:17:38,177
You watched while hands were laid on me!

695
01:17:38,968 --> 01:17:41,302
You watched while my honor
was dragged through the streets!

696
01:17:41,885 --> 01:17:44,177
As a father, you've done nothing for me.

697
01:17:51,302 --> 01:17:54,843
Be it the man
who fathered me, or his wife…

698
01:17:55,468 --> 01:17:57,593
Whoever stands against me…

699
01:18:17,093 --> 01:18:22,510
After all this time, I finally see
my family truly is and who isn't.

700
01:18:25,427 --> 01:18:26,968
I'm telling you, as your aunt.

701
01:18:29,260 --> 01:18:30,843
Hack him down, Rudra!

702
01:19:42,802 --> 01:19:45,010
There's the bugger you wanted.

703
01:19:46,218 --> 01:19:47,177
Hey, Rudra!

704
01:19:47,760 --> 01:19:51,593
I thought you'd die
that day in Bhairavakona.

705
01:19:52,052 --> 01:19:54,760
But today…
Even if the Goddess herself descends,

706
01:19:54,927 --> 01:19:57,677
she cannot save you or your family!

707
01:19:58,093 --> 01:19:59,052
Nephew!

708
01:20:00,052 --> 01:20:01,552
Drag her here!

709
01:21:56,218 --> 01:21:58,718
Hey! Bind him up!

710
01:22:02,843 --> 01:22:04,635
- Rudra!
- Brother!

711
01:22:10,802 --> 01:22:11,927
Rudra!

712
01:22:12,968 --> 01:22:15,802
Rudra! He's no ordinary man!

713
01:22:15,927 --> 01:22:18,677
- A demon! You saw it yourself.
- It's the truth.

714
01:22:19,093 --> 01:22:22,051
He turned your village
into a sea of blood.

715
01:22:22,052 --> 01:22:23,135
- No!
- Listen to me.

716
01:22:23,343 --> 01:22:25,176
Tell me where the Sacred Lotus is!

717
01:22:25,177 --> 01:22:26,092
Speak!

718
01:22:26,093 --> 01:22:28,217
Had I known,
I'd have brought it long ago!

719
01:22:28,218 --> 01:22:29,842
This won't make him speak.

720
01:22:29,843 --> 01:22:31,968
Stab him! That'll do it!

721
01:22:33,052 --> 01:22:34,635
- Brother-in law!
- Hey!

722
01:22:35,843 --> 01:22:37,718
Rudra! Rudra!

723
01:22:37,843 --> 01:22:41,427
Someone save him! Oh, God!

724
01:22:41,635 --> 01:22:44,010
- Do you want me to kill them all?
- My--

725
01:22:46,885 --> 01:22:50,135
- Oh, dear!
- My love--

726
01:23:03,468 --> 01:23:04,427
Hey!

727
01:23:12,635 --> 01:23:13,468
Mother!

728
01:23:13,593 --> 01:23:18,218
How can you just stand there
like a statue after seeing all this?

729
01:23:20,385 --> 01:23:21,510
Alas!

730
01:23:21,760 --> 01:23:22,927
Stop!

731
01:23:23,177 --> 01:23:25,010
You think you are
a great devotee like Prahlada?

732
01:23:25,927 --> 01:23:28,885
Call upon your savior then!

733
01:23:30,927 --> 01:23:32,093
Let me see!

734
01:23:32,635 --> 01:23:34,010
Hey!

735
01:23:34,927 --> 01:23:37,010
- No!
- Leave her!

736
01:23:37,968 --> 01:23:39,885
Mother!

737
01:23:51,593 --> 01:23:52,552
Anyway…

738
01:23:53,468 --> 01:23:56,218
For the Lord to descend on earth…

739
01:23:56,927 --> 01:23:59,093
This is not the era of Kalki…

740
01:24:00,468 --> 01:24:01,468
It's Kali's era!

741
01:24:02,885 --> 01:24:03,885
My era!

742
01:24:13,343 --> 01:24:15,302
No matter how many births I take…

743
01:24:16,010 --> 01:24:17,635
It is all for my own desire.

744
01:24:19,010 --> 01:24:22,760
Until my wish is fulfilled…
I shall keep returning.

745
01:24:23,427 --> 01:24:26,051
What will make you
handover the Sacred Lotus?

746
01:24:26,052 --> 01:24:28,593
No matter how many lives you take…

747
01:24:29,218 --> 01:24:32,927
The truth will never leave his lips, sir.

748
01:24:33,093 --> 01:24:35,801
Like the sorcerer's life
hidden in a parrot…

749
01:24:35,802 --> 01:24:38,343
His life rests within that bird.

750
01:24:43,885 --> 01:24:46,885
- ♪ I'll give you stallions to ride ♪
- Hey!

751
01:24:49,718 --> 01:24:50,677
Hey!

752
01:24:53,593 --> 01:24:55,842
- Hey! Leave my sister!
- Please let Manasa go.

753
01:24:55,843 --> 01:24:58,552
Your sister is your very life, is she not?

754
01:24:59,593 --> 01:25:04,010
Will you speak now or shall I kill her?

755
01:25:08,635 --> 01:25:10,052
Brother!

756
01:25:18,427 --> 01:25:19,427
Hey!

757
01:25:23,802 --> 01:25:25,093
Brother!

758
01:26:07,385 --> 01:26:08,927
Brother!

759
01:27:34,302 --> 01:27:35,135
Hey.

760
01:27:49,927 --> 01:27:50,885
Kill him!

761
01:28:13,010 --> 01:28:13,843
Hey!

762
01:30:57,760 --> 01:31:03,343
♪ Are You there or not, O Eshwara? ♪

763
01:31:04,385 --> 01:31:10,677
♪ If You are, what divine drama? ♪

764
01:31:10,802 --> 01:31:17,052
♪ You are a God who cannot guard or save ♪

765
01:31:17,218 --> 01:31:23,385
♪ Is all this sin
Your share to brave? ♪

766
01:31:23,510 --> 01:31:30,260
♪ For us
Is birth itself a chain, a curse? ♪

767
01:31:30,468 --> 01:31:34,718
♪ O Eshwara ♪

768
01:31:36,802 --> 01:31:39,885
- ♪ For You, is the funeral fire ♪
- Hey, wait!

769
01:31:40,510 --> 01:31:43,593
♪ Salvation's verse? ♪

770
01:31:43,760 --> 01:31:47,052
♪ O Eternal One ♪

771
01:31:49,885 --> 01:31:53,677
♪ Time itself… ♪

772
01:32:01,593 --> 01:32:08,135
- My life.
- ♪ Like poison fell ♪

773
01:32:09,343 --> 01:32:10,302
Sister!

774
01:32:16,135 --> 01:32:22,510
♪ Time itself, like poison fell
Carving wounds so deep ♪

775
01:32:22,635 --> 01:32:29,342
♪ Silence turned a lullaby
Asking me no reply to keep ♪

776
01:32:29,343 --> 01:32:32,510
♪ Time itself like poison fell ♪

777
01:32:32,635 --> 01:32:35,842
♪ Carving wounds so deep ♪

778
01:32:35,843 --> 01:32:42,968
♪ Silence turned a lullaby
Asking me no reply to keep ♪

779
01:32:57,552 --> 01:32:58,677
What do you say?

780
01:32:58,843 --> 01:33:00,302
My love--

781
01:33:09,010 --> 01:33:12,135
♪ Eshwara! ♪

782
01:33:13,385 --> 01:33:17,468
♪ Eshwara! ♪

783
01:33:47,843 --> 01:33:49,343
Hey, Shiva!

784
01:33:49,677 --> 01:33:51,093
My name isn't Shiva.

785
01:33:52,093 --> 01:33:53,052
It's Rudra!

786
01:33:53,718 --> 01:33:55,218
They're both the same.

787
01:33:55,468 --> 01:33:58,593
When he lets go, he's Rudra.
When he embraces, he's Shiva.

788
01:33:58,760 --> 01:34:00,260
That's the only difference.

789
01:34:01,343 --> 01:34:04,218
What is it? Thinking too much?

790
01:34:04,593 --> 01:34:06,052
Or drowning in sorrow?

791
01:34:08,510 --> 01:34:11,135
When your dreams burn
before your eyes,

792
01:34:11,593 --> 01:34:13,552
faith begins to slip away.

793
01:34:13,718 --> 01:34:17,510
Only the one who holds on tight
can keep from falling apart.

794
01:34:17,635 --> 01:34:21,260
Swami, death is what gives beauty to life.

795
01:34:21,427 --> 01:34:26,635
But man fails to understand that
and keeps chasing worldly attachments.

796
01:34:29,385 --> 01:34:31,593
He grants nine months for birth

797
01:34:31,968 --> 01:34:34,718
but he can snatch it away in an instant.

798
01:34:35,218 --> 01:34:37,052
Have you ever wondered why?

799
01:34:37,260 --> 01:34:40,759
Because if death came with a warning,

800
01:34:40,760 --> 01:34:44,427
man would spend his whole life
destroying himself in fear.

801
01:34:45,135 --> 01:34:46,677
That's what I'm afraid of.

802
01:34:47,135 --> 01:34:48,218
Swami!

803
01:34:49,385 --> 01:34:52,177
Life is about moving forward
while holding onto memories

804
01:34:53,135 --> 01:34:57,343
of the departed and searching
for unanswered questions!

805
01:34:58,052 --> 01:34:59,177
Swami!

806
01:34:59,593 --> 01:35:02,552
Even Shiva himself, smeared in sacred ash,

807
01:35:03,135 --> 01:35:08,593
he didn't perish with his beloved
when he lost her to the flames, Swami.

808
01:35:10,427 --> 01:35:13,718
He sought the reason behind it
and destroyed everyone responsible.

809
01:35:16,093 --> 01:35:19,677
"I don't want this war! I won't fight it!"

810
01:35:19,843 --> 01:35:22,760
When Arjuna tried
to walk away in detachment…

811
01:35:24,843 --> 01:35:27,677
didn't Lord Krishna
bring him back to Kurukshetra?

812
01:35:29,593 --> 01:35:31,718
What you do for yourself is duty.

813
01:35:32,343 --> 01:35:34,593
What you do for others is righteousness.

814
01:35:35,260 --> 01:35:39,093
Grieving endlessly
over the dead is futile.

815
01:35:39,677 --> 01:35:43,260
Because you came into this world alone,

816
01:35:43,510 --> 01:35:45,385
and you'll leave it alone too.

817
01:35:46,760 --> 01:35:47,677
Swami.

818
01:35:48,135 --> 01:35:50,510
Do you know
what truly lasts forever in this world?

819
01:35:52,427 --> 01:35:54,468
Truth shall be your mother,

820
01:35:55,135 --> 01:35:57,343
wisdom your father,

821
01:35:57,635 --> 01:35:59,718
righteousness is your sibling,

822
01:36:00,052 --> 01:36:02,010
compassion is your friend,

823
01:36:02,260 --> 01:36:04,260
peace is your wife

824
01:36:04,552 --> 01:36:06,843
and forgiveness is your child.

825
01:36:09,135 --> 01:36:10,677
Only these six are eternal.

826
01:36:11,177 --> 01:36:13,968
Everything else is temporary.

827
01:36:20,177 --> 01:36:23,427
Time will tell you why you were born.

828
01:36:24,718 --> 01:36:28,718
But only you can discover
the meaning of your birth.

829
01:36:29,968 --> 01:36:30,968
You'll find it.

830
01:36:32,302 --> 01:36:35,802
Rudra… you'll find your path.

831
01:36:36,310 --> 01:36:36,862
Yeah.

832
01:36:39,843 --> 01:36:45,302
♪ Lord of Ashes, O Linga
What is this divine play of yours? ♪

833
01:36:50,302 --> 01:36:51,135
Parvathi.

834
01:36:53,552 --> 01:36:55,552
Do you know why I'm actually here?

835
01:36:57,968 --> 01:37:00,510
- The Sacred Lotus…
- Tell me where it is.

836
01:37:06,385 --> 01:37:09,552
- It is known as Sacred Lotus.
- Some guy from town named Shera.

837
01:37:12,718 --> 01:37:14,260
You'll find your path.

838
01:37:15,802 --> 01:37:17,510
Have you seen the Sacred Lotus?

839
01:37:19,510 --> 01:37:21,593
She and Shera are missing.

840
01:38:06,677 --> 01:38:08,635
Poor soul. How did he die?

841
01:38:09,052 --> 01:38:13,177
He falsely accused Achyutachari,
who had done nothing wrong.

842
01:38:13,302 --> 01:38:14,302
He's gone.

843
01:38:26,093 --> 01:38:29,635
- I knew you would come.
- They destroyed our entire settlement.

844
01:38:30,343 --> 01:38:33,093
They took away everyone
I ever called my own.

845
01:38:33,885 --> 01:38:35,468
They reduced our lives to ashes.

846
01:38:36,677 --> 01:38:38,177
All for that Sacred Lotus…

847
01:38:41,135 --> 01:38:45,052
They killed my sister
under a wedding canopy.

848
01:38:48,593 --> 01:38:50,343
They turned my mother into a corpse.

849
01:38:53,093 --> 01:38:56,385
They drowned the entire village
in blood, even innocent children.

850
01:38:57,677 --> 01:38:58,635
Mom!

851
01:38:59,052 --> 01:39:01,593
What's your connection to Shera,
the man behind this massacre?

852
01:39:02,427 --> 01:39:06,093
We have… nothing to do with Shera.

853
01:39:08,843 --> 01:39:10,593
The reason behind all this…

854
01:39:24,927 --> 01:39:26,552
Their arrival that day…

855
01:39:27,177 --> 01:39:31,177
ruined our lives
and disgraced our lineage.

856
01:39:32,135 --> 01:39:34,635
You're not asking for help to do good.

857
01:39:35,427 --> 01:39:37,760
You're asking me to aid a wrongdoing.

858
01:39:38,343 --> 01:39:40,760
That will never happen,
even if I lose my life.

859
01:39:51,343 --> 01:39:52,802
Ravi Varma…

860
01:39:54,302 --> 01:39:57,427
You may set and rise again, like the sun.

861
01:39:59,385 --> 01:40:01,635
But your bloodline… your children…

862
01:40:02,552 --> 01:40:04,427
once they perish…

863
01:40:05,885 --> 01:40:07,510
they'll never rise again.

864
01:40:11,968 --> 01:40:15,010
Anyone can bring the temple key.

865
01:40:15,343 --> 01:40:19,468
But only Achyutachari
can open the temple doors.

866
01:40:20,260 --> 01:40:22,468
Achyuta? Who is he?

867
01:40:23,177 --> 01:40:27,051
He's the temple's chief priest.
Only he knows the secret.

868
01:40:27,052 --> 01:40:30,343
Not even the fear of death
could make him speak.

869
01:40:31,468 --> 01:40:35,677
- Then how do we make him talk?
- Earn his trust.

870
01:40:37,635 --> 01:40:39,718
Trust cuts deeper than fear.

871
01:40:41,593 --> 01:40:42,843
Make him trust you.

872
01:40:45,552 --> 01:40:47,135
As part of the plan,

873
01:40:47,510 --> 01:40:51,385
Parvathi entered Achyutachari's family.

874
01:40:52,093 --> 01:40:55,635
She got close to them
and earned everyone's trust.

875
01:40:56,385 --> 01:41:00,260
To keep themselves informed
of every event…

876
01:41:01,468 --> 01:41:03,218
They sent Shera to us.

877
01:41:05,635 --> 01:41:09,927
Parvati, having uncovered the secret
of the lock that no one else knew,

878
01:41:10,177 --> 01:41:12,302
on the final night of the festivities…

879
01:41:46,052 --> 01:41:47,177
But

880
01:41:47,677 --> 01:41:49,968
carrying a god is
easier than…

881
01:41:51,442 --> 01:41:52,442
stealing one.

882
01:41:55,927 --> 01:41:57,552
- Hello.-Ravi Varma.

883
01:41:57,677 --> 01:41:59,593
The plane crashed near Bhairavakona.

884
01:42:00,343 --> 01:42:02,177
The Sacred Lotus
remains inside the wreckage.

885
01:42:02,385 --> 01:42:03,927
Tell Parvathi immediately.

886
01:42:07,927 --> 01:42:09,718
It was for that Sacred Lotus

887
01:42:09,843 --> 01:42:13,052
that Parvathi and Shera
came to your hamlet.

888
01:42:23,177 --> 01:42:25,343
I don't know what happened

889
01:42:25,552 --> 01:42:28,927
after Parvathi and Shera
reached your village.

890
01:42:29,635 --> 01:42:30,337
But,

891
01:42:32,927 --> 01:42:34,968
if you want to know the whole truth

892
01:42:35,510 --> 01:42:37,635
you must first find Parvathi.

893
01:42:44,343 --> 01:42:46,468
Go straight and turn right.

894
01:43:18,093 --> 01:43:19,052
Guruji!

895
01:43:21,968 --> 01:43:23,177
Parvathi, my dear!

896
01:43:23,468 --> 01:43:25,760
What happened? Tell me!

897
01:43:29,552 --> 01:43:32,135
- Forgive me, Guruji.
- What happened, child?

898
01:43:33,218 --> 01:43:35,843
- What happened?
- I must tell you the truth.

899
01:43:38,093 --> 01:43:42,302
The one who stole the Sacred Lotus
was none other than… me.

900
01:43:46,635 --> 01:43:50,385
You'd have heard
tales of demons in legends

901
01:43:50,927 --> 01:43:52,593
and read about them in books.

902
01:43:53,635 --> 01:43:56,385
But I saw one with my own eyes.

903
01:43:57,927 --> 01:44:00,802
That demon is Zulfiqar Ali.

904
01:44:02,135 --> 01:44:04,885
It was because of him
that I committed this terrible act.

905
01:44:05,552 --> 01:44:07,552
I never did it willingly, Guruji.

906
01:44:08,802 --> 01:44:10,093
Please forgive me.

907
01:44:10,968 --> 01:44:12,343
Please forgive me.

908
01:44:15,218 --> 01:44:18,677
Mr. Prabhakar,
the Indian Archaeology Department Chief…

909
01:44:19,718 --> 01:44:20,635
was my father.

910
01:44:22,843 --> 01:44:26,093
My sister Revathi, Tesla,
and Zulfiqar Ali…

911
01:44:26,635 --> 01:44:28,968
were all archaeology students together.

912
01:44:32,135 --> 01:44:35,468
My sister and Tesla
fell in love with each other.

913
01:44:39,552 --> 01:44:42,802
Since Tesla is a Britisher,
my father didn't approve.

914
01:44:44,093 --> 01:44:48,427
So they got married
without his knowledge.

915
01:44:54,135 --> 01:44:56,177
- Yeah, sure. Hi, Parvathi.
- Stop!

916
01:44:59,135 --> 01:45:00,885
You married against my wishes.

917
01:45:01,427 --> 01:45:02,760
Go wherever you please.

918
01:45:09,052 --> 01:45:09,677
Sister!

919
01:45:12,510 --> 01:45:14,510
Unable to forget what my sister did,

920
01:45:14,760 --> 01:45:18,802
father stopped going to work
and shut himself away in grief.

921
01:45:19,135 --> 01:45:20,968
- Some time later…
- [phone rings]

922
01:45:21,093 --> 01:45:21,927
What?!

923
01:45:23,427 --> 01:45:26,343
Congratulations! Are you serious?

924
01:45:27,427 --> 01:45:30,052
Dad! you're going to be a granddad.

925
01:45:32,218 --> 01:45:34,427
The moment he learned he had
a granddaughter,

926
01:45:34,635 --> 01:45:36,760
he invited them home.

927
01:45:38,760 --> 01:45:39,884
Grandpa!

928
01:45:39,885 --> 01:45:42,802
After that, Riya became his whole world.

929
01:45:45,052 --> 01:45:46,177
Grandpa!

930
01:46:01,218 --> 01:46:03,968
My father's love for Riya grew stronger,

931
01:46:04,468 --> 01:46:06,677
but his anger toward
Tesla never faded.

932
01:46:07,177 --> 01:46:08,635
Driven by that anger,

933
01:46:08,927 --> 01:46:12,927
my father entrusted Ali with finding
the Temple of the Virata Purusha

934
01:46:13,177 --> 01:46:14,843
and asked him to assist Tesla.

935
01:46:15,177 --> 01:46:18,885
Tesla found the Nagabandham scripture
during that research.

936
01:46:19,218 --> 01:46:22,552
Realizing Ali would come
for the Nagabandham scripture at any cost…

937
01:46:22,718 --> 01:46:25,010
Sir, I only trust you.

938
01:46:26,718 --> 01:46:28,760
India's future is in your hands.

939
01:46:34,510 --> 01:46:36,885
Please let us go, Uncle!

940
01:46:43,468 --> 01:46:45,218
Daddy!

941
01:46:46,468 --> 01:46:47,509
Daddy!

942
01:46:47,510 --> 01:46:49,635
- Riya, my dear…
- Grandpa!

943
01:46:49,927 --> 01:46:51,552
- Come here.
- Grandpa.

944
01:46:54,010 --> 01:46:56,135
Grandpa… Mommy!

945
01:46:58,510 --> 01:46:59,968
Mommy…

946
01:47:02,552 --> 01:47:05,302
Grandpa, he hit mommy.

947
01:47:06,052 --> 01:47:07,634
- Revathi!
- Mommy.

948
01:47:07,635 --> 01:47:09,177
Robert! Revathi!

949
01:47:12,552 --> 01:47:14,968
Robert! Hey! Hey!

950
01:47:15,510 --> 01:47:17,635
- Revathi…
- Dad! Dad!

951
01:47:17,968 --> 01:47:19,343
Rev-- Revathi!

952
01:47:19,593 --> 01:47:22,593
- Revathi! You…
- What kind of people are you?

953
01:47:23,302 --> 01:47:27,760
You never showed this love
while they were alive.

954
01:47:28,927 --> 01:47:30,760
Did it appear only after they died?!

955
01:47:31,177 --> 01:47:32,093
Hey!

956
01:47:36,135 --> 01:47:38,635
This is the book you wanted, right?

957
01:47:42,135 --> 01:47:44,760
Take it and let my Grandpa go.

958
01:47:45,302 --> 01:47:48,385
Please, Uncle. Let us go.

959
01:47:56,635 --> 01:47:58,510
- Revathi, my child!
- Dad!

960
01:48:00,135 --> 01:48:03,635
- You won't have to be angry anymore…
- No.

961
01:48:05,468 --> 01:48:07,593
I won't be there either.

962
01:48:08,218 --> 01:48:10,093
Dear Revathi!

963
01:48:10,260 --> 01:48:12,552
My baby… Ba--

964
01:48:13,093 --> 01:48:16,218
- Take… care of her, Dad.
- Don't say that.

965
01:48:17,093 --> 01:48:19,843
- Mommy! Mommy!
- Revathi.

966
01:48:20,010 --> 01:48:23,052
- Revathi, my child!
- Mommy! No!

967
01:48:25,093 --> 01:48:26,218
Hey, Ali!

968
01:48:27,052 --> 01:48:29,468
If the Serpent seal
is like a Lotus formation,

969
01:48:30,427 --> 01:48:34,093
the scripture in your hand is
an Abhimanyu!

970
01:48:35,218 --> 01:48:38,385
It will only show you the way in!

971
01:48:43,010 --> 01:48:44,968
Grandpa!

972
01:48:48,177 --> 01:48:52,135
So… you're the solution
to find my way back.

973
01:48:54,968 --> 01:48:56,010
Later on,

974
01:48:56,343 --> 01:48:58,677
my father found out that Sacred Lotus

975
01:48:58,885 --> 01:49:01,802
is in Srirangapuram
through Nagabandham scripture.

976
01:49:02,302 --> 01:49:03,510
But…

977
01:49:04,093 --> 01:49:05,968
my conscience wouldn't allow me…

978
01:49:07,635 --> 01:49:09,635
to steal the Sacred Lotus.

979
01:49:12,552 --> 01:49:14,218
At that moment…

980
01:49:28,427 --> 01:49:30,302
Riya!
Riya!

981
01:49:33,635 --> 01:49:35,718
Bringing it here isn't that easy.

982
01:49:36,052 --> 01:49:36,885
And Riya?

983
01:49:40,927 --> 01:49:42,593
She misses you a lot.

984
01:49:44,010 --> 01:49:46,218
The longer you delay,
the greater the danger.

985
01:49:55,843 --> 01:49:56,760
Dad…

986
01:49:57,302 --> 01:50:00,010
this isn't just wrong… it's a sin.

987
01:50:01,052 --> 01:50:03,052
I don't know where this will lead us.

988
01:50:03,718 --> 01:50:05,218
When something becomes unavoidable,

989
01:50:05,843 --> 01:50:08,552
we can't think about right and wrong.

990
01:50:10,260 --> 01:50:11,843
When the intention is pure,

991
01:50:12,885 --> 01:50:15,760
one who accepts
even poison as nectar is God.

992
01:50:17,385 --> 01:50:19,052
He will understand.

993
01:50:22,718 --> 01:50:25,760
Even asking for forgiveness
feels like a grave sin now.

994
01:50:27,260 --> 01:50:31,802
We desecrated a sacred temple
for our own selfish needs.

995
01:50:33,885 --> 01:50:37,177
- And I framed you for it.
- You should be killed.

996
01:50:40,385 --> 01:50:43,468
- Rudra?
- You drove him away from the temple.

997
01:50:44,010 --> 01:50:46,427
You took away everyone I had.

998
01:50:47,260 --> 01:50:48,343
Rudra!

999
01:50:50,010 --> 01:50:52,760
I had nothing to do
with that massacre, Rudra.

1000
01:50:52,927 --> 01:50:55,968
I came to your village
only for the Sacred Lotus.

1001
01:50:56,885 --> 01:50:58,260
And I met you.

1002
01:50:58,927 --> 01:51:02,010
That day, no one who went
after the Sacred Lotus returned.

1003
01:51:02,552 --> 01:51:05,218
But I found you
lying injured on the shore.

1004
01:51:05,510 --> 01:51:07,968
I searched you,
thinking you might have it.

1005
01:51:08,093 --> 01:51:09,093
But it wasn't there.

1006
01:51:09,468 --> 01:51:11,635
You were the only one
who knew anything about it.

1007
01:51:12,052 --> 01:51:13,343
That's why I saved you.

1008
01:51:13,843 --> 01:51:17,552
I tried many times to ask you about it
after you regained consciousness.

1009
01:51:18,677 --> 01:51:21,302
But before that could happen
the tragedy unfolded.

1010
01:51:21,677 --> 01:51:23,010
Why have you come now?

1011
01:51:28,427 --> 01:51:30,427
We brought
you the Sacred Lotus you wanted.

1012
01:51:30,927 --> 01:51:33,885
Where is our Riya?
Return my granddaughter to me.

1013
01:51:37,177 --> 01:51:39,052
It's not over yet, Prabhakar.

1014
01:51:39,385 --> 01:51:41,260
There's one small task left.

1015
01:51:41,718 --> 01:51:44,010
What else is left now except destruction?

1016
01:51:47,260 --> 01:51:50,677
The very land I once walked with pride,

1017
01:51:52,302 --> 01:51:55,052
the culture I spoke of with honor,

1018
01:51:55,593 --> 01:51:58,552
you made me betray that very soil.

1019
01:51:58,802 --> 01:51:59,843
Hey!

1020
01:52:00,010 --> 01:52:01,802
You burned down the village,

1021
01:52:02,885 --> 01:52:04,760
and slaughtered innocent people.

1022
01:52:06,885 --> 01:52:10,010
Using a little girl's life as leverage,

1023
01:52:10,718 --> 01:52:14,552
you turned a patriot into a traitor.

1024
01:52:15,218 --> 01:52:17,426
What more is left now?

1025
01:52:17,427 --> 01:52:19,302
Tell me! What else is left?!

1026
01:52:19,635 --> 01:52:22,218
- What else?!
- Ali…

1027
01:52:22,552 --> 01:52:25,802
Please let us go.
We can't endure this anymore.

1028
01:52:25,968 --> 01:52:27,760
Kill both of us if you want!

1029
01:52:28,052 --> 01:52:30,010
But please spare Riya.

1030
01:52:30,427 --> 01:52:32,468
Ever since we obeyed you,

1031
01:52:32,593 --> 01:52:38,135
every moment of our lives
has felt like breathing poison.

1032
01:52:39,677 --> 01:52:42,135
After witnessing so much betrayal
and so many deaths…

1033
01:52:42,260 --> 01:52:45,051
What is even left for us to live for?

1034
01:52:45,052 --> 01:52:48,635
We can't take this anymore.
Show us some mercy.

1035
01:52:50,218 --> 01:52:52,843
There's only one thing
this Abdali doesn't know.

1036
01:52:53,468 --> 01:52:55,052
Mercy.

1037
01:52:57,302 --> 01:52:58,968
I need one final thing from you.

1038
01:52:59,468 --> 01:53:01,635
Please understand.

1039
01:53:02,552 --> 01:53:03,968
He wants the Garuda mantras!

1040
01:53:04,802 --> 01:53:07,427
We'll stay alive
only if we hand them over to Ali.

1041
01:53:11,635 --> 01:53:13,593
Only you can save us, Guruji.

1042
01:53:33,093 --> 01:53:35,635
Salutations to Shiva and Vishnu
each the reflection of the other.

1043
01:53:37,302 --> 01:53:39,177
Our ancestors used to say
that along with the Sacred Lotus,

1044
01:53:39,760 --> 01:53:43,427
these palm-leaf scriptures,
were also entrusted to us by sages.

1045
01:53:43,968 --> 01:53:46,552
I believe you alone
will restore the Sacred Lotus,

1046
01:53:47,468 --> 01:53:50,052
to Lord Ranganatha's navel, son.

1047
01:53:51,385 --> 01:53:52,343
Here.

1048
01:53:57,177 --> 01:53:58,385
May victory be yours.

1049
01:54:02,593 --> 01:54:04,218
Bhairagi!

1050
01:56:26,760 --> 01:56:27,843
Leave me!

1051
01:56:29,468 --> 01:56:30,510
Grandpa!

1052
01:56:31,677 --> 01:56:32,552
Riya!

1053
01:56:33,093 --> 01:56:35,552
- My dear Riya!
- Grandpa!

1054
01:56:36,593 --> 01:56:38,302
- Riya!
- Grandpa!

1055
01:56:38,510 --> 01:56:39,718
Riya!

1056
01:56:40,552 --> 01:56:42,218
Dear Riya!

1057
01:57:45,552 --> 01:57:48,177
The Serpent seal is being unlocked!

1058
01:57:49,885 --> 01:57:51,718
A dream I cherished for years…

1059
01:57:53,343 --> 01:57:56,302
is finally becoming reality today.

1060
01:57:58,718 --> 01:58:00,093
Abdali!

1061
01:58:01,510 --> 01:58:04,343
The time to rule the universe

1062
01:58:05,510 --> 01:58:07,177
is drawing near.

1063
01:58:09,302 --> 01:58:12,218
The eclipse full moon is approaching.

1064
01:58:12,968 --> 01:58:15,635
The Serpent seal will be unlocked!

1065
01:58:18,802 --> 01:58:20,802
Now all that's left,

1066
01:58:21,927 --> 01:58:24,552
is to get my hands on the Garuda mantras.

1067
01:58:24,927 --> 01:58:27,593
Soon they'll be in your hands, Bhairagi.

1068
01:58:28,635 --> 01:58:30,468
Once the Garuda mantras arrive,

1069
01:58:31,052 --> 01:58:35,802
you reciting them will open
the Serpent sealed gate,

1070
01:58:35,927 --> 01:58:37,385
and we'll step inside…

1071
01:58:37,552 --> 01:58:39,968
everything will happen
as planned, Bhairagi.

1072
01:58:43,218 --> 01:58:44,177
Fool!

1073
01:58:48,218 --> 01:58:51,468
To protect righteousness, in every age,

1074
01:58:52,093 --> 01:58:54,135
in whatever form he must take,

1075
01:58:56,052 --> 01:58:58,635
however many times he must be reborn,

1076
01:59:00,052 --> 01:59:01,927
the Lord will always return.

1077
01:59:04,052 --> 01:59:05,885
And he will stop demons like you

1078
01:59:06,593 --> 01:59:09,468
from entering that divine gateway.

1079
01:59:12,802 --> 01:59:15,718
Kali controls the Time now, Prabhakar.

1080
01:59:16,260 --> 01:59:19,885
No one can stop our mission anymore.

1081
01:59:20,343 --> 01:59:21,510
No one is coming.

1082
01:59:26,760 --> 01:59:28,093
Grandpa!

1083
01:59:31,635 --> 01:59:33,635
Grandpa!

1084
02:00:02,260 --> 02:00:03,885
Aunt!

1085
02:00:04,093 --> 02:00:06,010
Grandpa!

1086
02:00:06,552 --> 02:00:07,427
Riya!

1087
02:00:31,635 --> 02:00:33,552
Dad! Dad!

1088
02:00:34,427 --> 02:00:37,052
Grandpa, please!

1089
02:00:37,385 --> 02:00:38,552
Dad…

1090
02:01:01,570 --> 02:01:03,278
Hey!

1091
02:01:39,052 --> 02:01:41,343
Shiva!

1092
02:02:24,552 --> 02:02:25,427
Please, come.

1093
02:02:29,385 --> 02:02:31,343
- Greetings.
- Greetings, Swami.

1094
02:02:31,552 --> 02:02:33,759
What do you have
in your hands, little one?

1095
02:02:33,760 --> 02:02:36,385
A Tulasi garland for the Lord.

1096
02:02:39,135 --> 02:02:40,677
May you live long!

1097
02:03:05,718 --> 02:03:07,510
Everyone get inside the gate!

1098
02:03:14,052 --> 02:03:16,593
Quick! Get inside!

1099
02:03:17,177 --> 02:03:18,635
Lord Ranganatha!

1100
02:03:31,802 --> 02:03:33,760
Move. Quickly!

1101
02:03:36,052 --> 02:03:37,052
Quickly!

1102
02:03:39,343 --> 02:03:40,802
Close the doors!

1103
02:03:41,010 --> 02:03:44,135
- Everyone, get inside!
- Mom! Mom!

1104
02:04:09,552 --> 02:04:10,885
Govinda!

1105
02:04:11,510 --> 02:04:14,427
Lord Ranganatha!
Please protect us.

1106
02:04:17,093 --> 02:04:18,510
Govinda!

1107
02:04:19,302 --> 02:04:20,885
Sir!

1108
02:04:22,802 --> 02:04:25,802
- Mom.
- They're kids, sir. I beg you.

1109
02:04:26,093 --> 02:04:27,677
Don't do this!

1110
02:04:27,885 --> 02:04:30,677
- I beg you. Spare them, sir.
- Mom.

1111
02:04:31,010 --> 02:04:31,927
Sir!

1112
02:04:33,135 --> 02:04:36,635
- Please, sir. Let her go.
- Please leave. Please leave!

1113
02:04:46,302 --> 02:04:47,302
Please leave us.

1114
02:05:07,885 --> 02:05:10,217
Protect this Sacred Lotus.
It will protect you.

1115
02:05:10,218 --> 02:05:11,509
- Okay…
- Go, child. Go!

1116
02:05:11,510 --> 02:05:12,760
Okay, Guruji.

1117
02:05:13,468 --> 02:05:14,302
Hurry.

1118
02:05:15,468 --> 02:05:16,385
Be careful.

1119
02:05:24,010 --> 02:05:26,760
Please protect us.
Narayana!

1120
02:05:27,177 --> 02:05:28,343
Oh Lord!

1121
02:05:31,885 --> 02:05:34,510
Please protect us, Lord!

1122
02:06:58,635 --> 02:07:00,052
[in Hindi] I found it!

1123
02:08:53,510 --> 02:08:55,843
Well done, Bhairagi!

1124
02:08:56,302 --> 02:08:57,968
Well done!

1125
02:09:11,802 --> 02:09:15,802
Every word you said… has come true.

1126
02:09:27,010 --> 02:09:30,885
Now I shall rule the world
with this treasure.

1127
02:09:32,177 --> 02:09:35,093
With the corpses of these Hindus,

1128
02:09:35,593 --> 02:09:37,218
I will spread fear.

1129
02:09:37,635 --> 02:09:41,593
I will plant our flag
on this nation's soil.

1130
02:09:43,510 --> 02:09:46,052
Tell me, Bhairagi, tell me!

1131
02:09:46,343 --> 02:09:47,593
What do you desire?

1132
02:09:50,010 --> 02:09:51,718
What are you searching for, Bhairagi?

1133
02:09:58,552 --> 02:10:00,427
The Sacred Lotus.

1134
02:10:04,385 --> 02:10:05,468
What's that?

1135
02:10:08,760 --> 02:10:12,385
This treasure can only rule the earth.

1136
02:10:13,510 --> 02:10:18,260
But… the Sacred Lotus
that rested upon the Lord's navel…

1137
02:10:22,718 --> 02:10:25,052
rules the entire universe!

1138
02:10:26,260 --> 02:10:30,552
- I want that Sacred Lotus!
- You will never obtain it, Bhairagi.

1139
02:10:36,468 --> 02:10:37,593
Hey!

1140
02:10:38,718 --> 02:10:40,385
You'll never get it.

1141
02:10:41,427 --> 02:10:43,135
You'll never get it!

1142
02:10:50,593 --> 02:10:51,843
Hey, Priest…

1143
02:10:52,718 --> 02:10:55,093
tell me where the Sacred Lotus is.

1144
02:10:57,093 --> 02:11:00,343
Ranganatha, death arrives
even when uninvited.

1145
02:11:02,843 --> 02:11:05,343
Do not summon it by force.

1146
02:11:05,802 --> 02:11:07,302
You fool!

1147
02:11:08,552 --> 02:11:12,177
- You cannot decide life and death.
- Hey!

1148
02:11:12,760 --> 02:11:15,635
Only the Supreme One can.

1149
02:11:16,218 --> 02:11:17,677
Without His command

1150
02:11:18,218 --> 02:11:22,218
nothing can occur
upon this earth He created!

1151
02:11:22,593 --> 02:11:23,718
Hey, Priest!

1152
02:11:25,302 --> 02:11:26,927
Where is your God?

1153
02:11:31,177 --> 02:11:32,010
Him?

1154
02:11:34,718 --> 02:11:38,467
Does this lifeless stone
really possess such power?

1155
02:11:38,468 --> 02:11:40,593
To you, it may seem like a mere stone.

1156
02:11:41,385 --> 02:11:43,635
But it is no stone. It's not!

1157
02:11:44,927 --> 02:11:47,010
It is the source of our very breath.

1158
02:11:47,218 --> 02:11:49,093
In the wind that blows everywhere

1159
02:11:49,260 --> 02:11:51,343
in the waters that flow…

1160
02:11:52,260 --> 02:11:53,635
in every single atom…

1161
02:11:54,468 --> 02:11:56,302
the Supreme dwells everywhere.

1162
02:11:57,385 --> 02:12:00,468
Is that so? In this stone?

1163
02:12:04,885 --> 02:12:07,093
When arrogance consumes your mind,

1164
02:12:07,885 --> 02:12:10,052
death devours you.

1165
02:12:11,052 --> 02:12:12,343
Your very nature

1166
02:12:13,135 --> 02:12:15,260
turns poisonous.

1167
02:12:16,718 --> 02:12:17,968
That is when man

1168
02:12:18,968 --> 02:12:21,010
starts believing he is God.

1169
02:12:21,468 --> 02:12:22,427
God!

1170
02:12:23,677 --> 02:12:25,427
God is the Creator.

1171
02:12:26,260 --> 02:12:27,927
For upholding dharma…

1172
02:12:28,968 --> 02:12:32,218
when demons like you obstruct the path…

1173
02:12:33,677 --> 02:12:35,260
When evil crosses all limits

1174
02:12:36,218 --> 02:12:37,760
to protect righteousness

1175
02:12:39,468 --> 02:12:45,885
God incarnates Himself
to destroy vile demons like you.

1176
02:12:48,343 --> 02:12:52,718
God will descend
for your destruction as well.

1177
02:12:54,052 --> 02:12:56,635
For every head you've severed,

1178
02:12:57,968 --> 02:13:00,760
for every temple you've destroyed

1179
02:13:01,010 --> 02:13:03,093
He will settle the score.

1180
02:13:04,177 --> 02:13:06,552
He will end your reign.

1181
02:13:09,760 --> 02:13:12,177
After slaughtering everyone here,

1182
02:13:13,302 --> 02:13:14,885
and forcing us to bow down,

1183
02:13:16,302 --> 02:13:21,010
that arrogant head of yours
is swollen with pride, isn't it?

1184
02:13:21,427 --> 02:13:22,885
He will sever it

1185
02:13:23,552 --> 02:13:26,885
and cast it
into the sacred fire of Sanatana Dharma.

1186
02:13:27,135 --> 02:13:29,427
You will turn to ash. Ash!

1187
02:14:57,302 --> 02:14:59,093
Shiva!

1188
02:15:13,010 --> 02:15:14,135
It's the Sacred Lotus!

1189
02:15:23,552 --> 02:15:25,760
[Sanskrit mantras]

1190
02:15:45,427 --> 02:15:48,343
♪ Timeless Bhairava
Blue-throated Lord of darkness ♪

1191
02:15:48,552 --> 02:15:51,093
♪ Om… ♪

1192
02:15:51,343 --> 02:15:54,343
♪ Three-eyed one with matted locks
Destroyer of time across all ages ♪

1193
02:15:54,468 --> 02:15:57,384
♪ Om… ♪

1194
02:15:57,385 --> 02:16:00,384
♪ With the thunderous beat of Damaru
His roaring rhythm shakes the heavens ♪

1195
02:16:00,385 --> 02:16:03,259
♪ He performs the fierce Tandava
May Lord Shiva bless us with peace ♪

1196
02:16:03,260 --> 02:16:04,801
♪ Destroyer of desire
Destroyer of cities ♪

1197
02:16:04,802 --> 02:16:06,342
♪ Destroyer of worldly bonds
Destroyer of sacrifice ♪

1198
02:16:06,343 --> 02:16:07,884
♪ Slayer of Gajasura
Destroyer of Andhaka ♪

1199
02:16:07,885 --> 02:16:09,552
♪ I bow to the One
Who destroys all darkness ♪

1200
02:16:09,677 --> 02:16:10,884
♪ Hara Hara Hara Hara Hara! ♪

1201
02:16:10,885 --> 02:16:13,260
♪ The storm clouds of war
Tear through the skies ♪

1202
02:16:15,635 --> 02:16:18,927
♪ Hara Hara Hara Hara Hara!
The gates of hell swing wide ♪

1203
02:16:21,635 --> 02:16:24,552
♪ Hara Hara Hara Hara!
A weapon forged for the great battle ♪

1204
02:16:24,677 --> 02:16:27,427
♪ Gham Gham Gham Gham Gham!
The force that crushes every calamity ♪

1205
02:16:27,635 --> 02:16:28,926
♪ Gana Gana Gana Gana Gana! ♪

1206
02:16:28,927 --> 02:16:32,260
♪ Bearers of the sacred Lingam
Devotees of Gangadhara ♪

1207
02:16:32,885 --> 02:16:35,677
♪ The Himalayas are His abode ♪

1208
02:16:35,885 --> 02:16:38,635
♪ Eternity echoes in His name ♪

1209
02:16:38,802 --> 02:16:41,677
♪ We worship, we surrender ♪

1210
02:16:41,927 --> 02:16:43,635
♪ Harom Hara! ♪

1211
02:16:44,802 --> 02:16:50,677
♪ The body itself is Shiva’s temple
Every atom is filled with Shiva ♪

1212
02:16:50,885 --> 02:16:55,052
♪ The Trident stands forever
As our shield and guiding force ♪

1213
02:17:00,052 --> 02:17:03,009
♪ Veera Naga
The secret army of Rudra ♪

1214
02:17:03,010 --> 02:17:05,967
♪ Vaira Naga
The doom that unleashes hell ♪

1215
02:17:05,968 --> 02:17:09,134
♪ Swaira Naga
The destiny of a thousand births ♪

1216
02:17:09,135 --> 02:17:11,967
♪ Fierce Naga! Divine Naga! ♪

1217
02:17:11,968 --> 02:17:14,968
♪ Veera Naga
The secret army of Rudra ♪

1218
02:17:15,093 --> 02:17:17,967
♪ Vaira Naga
The doom that unleashes hell ♪

1219
02:17:17,968 --> 02:17:21,092
♪ Swaira Naga
The destiny of a thousand births ♪

1220
02:17:21,093 --> 02:17:23,676
♪ Steadfast Naga! Supreme Naga! ♪

1221
02:17:23,677 --> 02:17:27,260
♪ Om! Salutations to Rudra
Salutations to the Mighty One ♪

1222
02:17:27,385 --> 02:17:30,426
♪ Salutations to Bhairava
Salutations to the Fierce One ♪

1223
02:17:30,427 --> 02:17:33,343
♪ Salutations to the Slayer of Time
Salutations to the Clad-in-Hide One ♪

1224
02:17:33,510 --> 02:17:36,343
♪ Salutations to the Lord of Beings
Salutations to the Embodiment of Time ♪

1225
02:17:36,510 --> 02:17:39,051
♪ Salutations to the Lord of Spirits
Salutations to the Master of All Life ♪

1226
02:17:39,052 --> 02:17:42,342
♪ Salutations to the Destroyer of Time
Salutations to the Blue-Throated One ♪

1227
02:17:42,343 --> 02:17:45,134
♪ Salutations to the Fearsome One
Salutations to the Benign One ♪

1228
02:17:45,135 --> 02:17:49,843
♪ Our endless reverence
To the Sky-Clad Lord ♪

1229
02:17:50,177 --> 02:17:51,843
Sacred…

1230
02:17:53,093 --> 02:17:54,885
Lotus…

1231
02:17:59,968 --> 02:18:00,927
Stop!

1232
02:18:07,385 --> 02:18:09,718
Our dharma is eternal.

1233
02:18:10,343 --> 02:18:12,885
Our deity is eternal.

1234
02:18:13,635 --> 02:18:16,468
Our lives are an offering to Lord Shiva.

1235
02:18:17,468 --> 02:18:20,052
Our courage lies
in protecting Hindu dharma.

1236
02:18:22,635 --> 02:18:26,260
Lord Shankara of Kailasa himself
descended as Kaladi Shankara…

1237
02:18:26,802 --> 02:18:30,385
The shield of protection
he bestowed upon this Vedic land…

1238
02:18:30,927 --> 02:18:33,093
is the Naga Sadhu way of life.

1239
02:18:36,010 --> 02:18:39,885
We have attained the supreme state
by inhaling within our breath,

1240
02:18:40,218 --> 02:18:44,635
the primal Rudra energies
that govern the cosmos itself.

1241
02:18:46,510 --> 02:18:48,927
This land is the abode of saffron.

1242
02:18:49,427 --> 02:18:50,927
A sanctuary of dharma.

1243
02:18:51,760 --> 02:18:55,177
Whenever Hindu society loses its way
and devotion weakens,

1244
02:18:55,635 --> 02:18:59,635
ours is the lineage of Adi Shankaracharya,

1245
02:19:00,427 --> 02:19:03,593
born from the union
of spiritual power and penance.

1246
02:19:07,427 --> 02:19:10,677
Hindutva is not a religion.
It is benevolence.

1247
02:19:11,427 --> 02:19:16,177
The destruction of the heretical forces
that seek to harm it…

1248
02:19:16,760 --> 02:19:18,218
is our sole purpose!

1249
02:19:28,510 --> 02:19:32,343
Endless madness is raging with arrogance.

1250
02:19:33,093 --> 02:19:36,843
It marched to spill blood
across this saffron land.

1251
02:19:39,135 --> 02:19:43,218
With the command of Adi Shankaracharya
and the blessings of Adiyogi,

1252
02:19:43,885 --> 02:19:46,260
let’s rip open the hearts
of those desert men!

1253
02:19:46,927 --> 02:19:49,885
If they so much as dream
of setting foot in these Himalayas,

1254
02:19:50,427 --> 02:19:52,843
we'll show them
not even their bones will be found!

1255
02:19:56,177 --> 02:19:57,801
Let's show them what happens

1256
02:19:57,802 --> 02:19:59,260
when this Vedic land
becomes a battlefield!

1257
02:20:01,218 --> 02:20:02,843
Let's prove that

1258
02:20:03,385 --> 02:20:05,843
heads are bound to roll
when Shiva's army marches!

1259
02:20:08,552 --> 02:20:11,843
Let us unleash the valor
of Sanatana Dharma in our blood

1260
02:20:12,302 --> 02:20:15,177
and dye the Himalayan snow
red with theirs!

1261
02:20:16,927 --> 02:20:19,885
For the protection of dharma,
let us all become Rudras of Time!

1262
02:20:21,218 --> 02:20:23,760
[in Sanskrit] This is the Eternal Dharma!

1263
02:20:24,010 --> 02:20:26,593
This is the Eternal Dharma!

1264
02:20:27,052 --> 02:20:29,801
Hara Hara Mahadev!

1265
02:20:29,802 --> 02:20:36,260
[all] Hara Hara Mahadev!

1266
02:20:38,718 --> 02:20:41,260
Is this the Sacred Lotus, Bhairagi?

1267
02:20:42,718 --> 02:20:44,843
Yes, this is it.
Yes, this is the one.

1268
02:20:45,593 --> 02:20:46,468
Wow!

1269
02:20:46,802 --> 02:20:49,217
Does this Sacred Lotus

1270
02:20:49,218 --> 02:20:52,552
truly possess the power
to rule the universe, Bhairagi?

1271
02:20:53,885 --> 02:20:54,802
Yes!

1272
02:20:55,718 --> 02:20:57,468
I can't believe it.

1273
02:20:58,468 --> 02:21:01,468
The universe doesn't run
on your belief, Abdali.

1274
02:21:03,468 --> 02:21:07,260
This Sacred Lotus is the key
to the great divine gateway,

1275
02:21:07,968 --> 02:21:09,718
created by Brahma.

1276
02:21:10,135 --> 02:21:13,427
By invoking Adisesha's serpent lineages,

1277
02:21:13,552 --> 02:21:18,135
the eight-direction mantra Serpent seal

1278
02:21:18,260 --> 02:21:19,677
is now released.

1279
02:21:35,343 --> 02:21:37,010
The Serpent seal?

1280
02:21:41,052 --> 02:21:42,385
[in Hindi] What is that?

1281
02:21:44,468 --> 02:21:47,760
To the north of the Himalayan peaks,

1282
02:21:48,218 --> 02:21:50,968
at the foothills of Mount Kailash,

1283
02:21:51,135 --> 02:21:53,843
there's the hidden temple
of that Virata Purusha.

1284
02:21:54,468 --> 02:21:55,510
Right there…

1285
02:21:55,927 --> 02:21:59,260
is the divine gateway
which was sealed by the Serpent seal.

1286
02:22:00,510 --> 02:22:03,135
After the Dwapara Yuga ended,

1287
02:22:03,343 --> 02:22:06,385
to prevent humans
from entering that gateway,

1288
02:22:06,552 --> 02:22:10,010
while the enlightened sages
performed a grand ritual

1289
02:22:10,302 --> 02:22:13,009
using their mystical powers
during the 200th full moon,

1290
02:22:13,010 --> 02:22:16,718
the Sacred Lotus
emerged from the sacred fire.

1291
02:22:23,718 --> 02:22:27,052
They sealed
the divine gateway with that ritual.

1292
02:22:27,510 --> 02:22:29,468
Fearing that evil forces in the Kali Yuga

1293
02:22:29,593 --> 02:22:32,802
might seize the Sacred Lotus
and open the gateway,

1294
02:22:33,010 --> 02:22:36,885
they invoked the most powerful serpents

1295
02:22:37,468 --> 02:22:39,218
and sealed it using the Serpent seal.

1296
02:22:39,885 --> 02:22:42,968
They inscribed the Garuda mantras,
used to unseal the Serpent seal,

1297
02:22:43,135 --> 02:22:46,260
in tantric script
upon palm-leaf manuscripts,

1298
02:22:46,510 --> 02:22:48,218
and placed the Sacred Lotus…

1299
02:22:48,968 --> 02:22:51,635
Install this Sacred Lotus

1300
02:22:52,177 --> 02:22:54,718
in the Sri Ranganatha Swamy temple.

1301
02:22:57,968 --> 02:23:00,927
They installed it in the foremost
among the 108 Vaishnava temples,

1302
02:23:01,093 --> 02:23:04,760
the Ranganatha Temple of Srirangapuram…

1303
02:23:07,427 --> 02:23:10,135
To unseal the Serpent seal,

1304
02:23:10,260 --> 02:23:14,052
we must install the Sacred Lotus
upon the golden pedestal,

1305
02:23:14,177 --> 02:23:18,760
and chant the Garuda mantras
before the 200th full moon.

1306
02:23:18,885 --> 02:23:21,760
Only then can
the divine gateway be opened.

1307
02:23:22,010 --> 02:23:23,468
Otherwise…

1308
02:23:29,802 --> 02:23:33,718
Anyway… what lies
beyond that gateway, Bhairagi?

1309
02:23:44,468 --> 02:23:45,677
[in Hindi] There are many here!

1310
02:24:35,718 --> 02:24:39,843
[Sanskrit mantra chanting]

1311
02:25:08,718 --> 02:25:10,677
What is happening, Bhairagi?

1312
02:25:10,968 --> 02:25:13,135
Prepare the army at once, Abdali.

1313
02:25:13,427 --> 02:25:16,677
We must leave this place immediately.
Take the Sacred Lotus.

1314
02:25:51,635 --> 02:25:52,843
♪ Hara! ♪

1315
02:25:53,510 --> 02:25:55,260
♪ Hara! Hara! ♪

1316
02:25:56,635 --> 02:25:58,010
♪ Hara! Hara! ♪

1317
02:26:07,552 --> 02:26:09,593
The Naga Sadhus…

1318
02:28:04,385 --> 02:28:06,801
♪ Veera Naga
The secret army of Rudra ♪

1319
02:28:06,802 --> 02:28:09,259
♪ Vaira Naga
The doom that unleashes hell ♪

1320
02:28:09,260 --> 02:28:11,801
♪ Swaira Naga
The destiny of a thousand births ♪

1321
02:28:11,802 --> 02:28:14,259
♪ Fierce Naga! Divine Naga! ♪

1322
02:28:14,260 --> 02:28:16,926
♪ Veera Naga
The secret army of Rudra ♪

1323
02:28:16,927 --> 02:28:19,093
♪ Vaira Naga
The doom that unleashes hell ♪

1324
02:28:19,260 --> 02:28:22,052
Hara Hara Mahadev!

1325
02:29:31,427 --> 02:29:33,593
Shiva!

1326
02:29:53,802 --> 02:29:55,635
Shiva!

1327
02:30:05,760 --> 02:30:07,593
Shiva!

1328
02:31:02,385 --> 02:31:03,677
Bhairagi!

1329
02:31:04,427 --> 02:31:09,635
Until you undo this serpent's seal,
no one can stop you.

1330
02:31:11,385 --> 02:31:12,343
Go!

1331
02:32:23,718 --> 02:32:24,759
Hey!

1332
02:32:24,760 --> 02:32:27,760
If you are the guardian
of this Serpent seal,

1333
02:32:27,885 --> 02:32:31,052
then I am the demon
who rules this earth!

1334
02:32:32,052 --> 02:32:37,302
I heard no one could get past
the Naga Sadhus and enter inside.

1335
02:32:38,927 --> 02:32:40,427
Well, he did.

1336
02:32:56,968 --> 02:33:02,302
[Sanskrit shloka]

1337
02:33:15,177 --> 02:33:19,135
[Sanskrit chanting continues]

1338
02:33:22,552 --> 02:33:26,135
You roam around
with ash smeared on your body.

1339
02:33:26,427 --> 02:33:27,593
You're worthless.

1340
02:33:28,552 --> 02:33:31,843
And what is your invisible God worth?

1341
02:33:37,885 --> 02:33:40,510
Are you mighty enough
to rule the five elements?

1342
02:33:41,760 --> 02:33:44,635
Though you destroyed our temples,

1343
02:33:45,385 --> 02:33:47,385
you cannot destroy our dharma.

1344
02:33:48,468 --> 02:33:50,593
We worship the Sun.

1345
02:33:52,177 --> 02:33:53,593
Can you stop it?

1346
02:33:56,260 --> 02:33:58,135
We worship the Earth.

1347
02:33:58,760 --> 02:34:00,177
Can you uproot it?

1348
02:34:03,510 --> 02:34:05,802
We worship the rivers.

1349
02:34:07,010 --> 02:34:08,552
Can you drain them?

1350
02:34:11,135 --> 02:34:13,260
We worship the forests.

1351
02:34:13,510 --> 02:34:15,343
Can you cut them all down?

1352
02:34:17,260 --> 02:34:19,593
The air we breathe is God.

1353
02:34:19,802 --> 02:34:22,010
The fire that burns is God.

1354
02:34:22,260 --> 02:34:25,802
God is the source
of this universe's salvation

1355
02:34:26,135 --> 02:34:28,218
and its annihilation.

1356
02:34:28,843 --> 02:34:29,843
Ultimately,

1357
02:34:30,468 --> 02:34:35,467
If you take our lives, the God who
gave us life will end His own.

1358
02:34:35,468 --> 02:34:36,885
Then call him here!

1359
02:36:22,677 --> 02:36:27,343
[in Sanskrit] Before the sacred idol
of Mahagaruda, all venom is subdued.

1360
02:37:33,927 --> 02:37:36,302
Destroyer and remover of poison,
let it be destroyed.

1361
02:37:37,510 --> 02:37:40,135
The poison has perished.
All of it has vanished.

1362
02:37:40,677 --> 02:37:43,593
The poison is destroyed,
the venom is slain.

1363
02:37:44,135 --> 02:37:46,468
By the sacred invocation,
the poison is vanquished.

1364
02:37:47,052 --> 02:37:49,802
May it be struck down
by Indra’s thunderbolt!

1365
02:38:07,593 --> 02:38:11,302
[in Sanskrit] Before the sacred idol
of Mahagaruda, all poison is subdued.

1366
02:38:47,510 --> 02:38:50,968
Hara Hara Mahadev!

1367
02:39:04,302 --> 02:39:06,301
[in Sanskrit] Move forth, move forth.

1368
02:39:06,302 --> 02:39:10,218
Doer of all deeds,
embodiment of every poison…

1369
02:39:11,385 --> 02:39:13,343
Corrupter of poison, nourisher of poison.

1370
02:39:30,218 --> 02:39:32,635
[in Sanskrit] Sever the serpent bonds.

1371
02:39:33,177 --> 02:39:35,218
Release us from the serpent’s snare.

1372
02:39:35,552 --> 02:39:37,677
Sever the serpent--

1373
02:40:34,510 --> 02:40:37,093
Bhairagi!

1374
02:41:16,093 --> 02:41:17,427
Riya!

1375
02:41:21,635 --> 02:41:23,302
Riya! Riya!

1376
02:41:27,086 --> 02:41:29,420
[Sanskrit chanting]

1377
02:41:41,302 --> 02:41:43,927
Revered in all three worlds.

1378
02:41:44,135 --> 02:41:47,343
The fierce and dreadful One,
blazing like the fire of doom.

1379
02:41:47,510 --> 02:41:49,093
To the Lord of adamantine claws!

1380
02:41:49,343 --> 02:41:51,093
The One with the mighty beak!

1381
02:42:00,760 --> 02:42:02,052
Riya! Are you okay?

1382
02:42:03,843 --> 02:42:04,760
Riya!

1383
02:42:05,052 --> 02:42:06,885
[in Sanskrit] Sever the serpent bonds.

1384
02:42:07,093 --> 02:42:09,593
Release us from the serpent’s snare.

1385
02:44:02,218 --> 02:44:04,468
Abdali! Abdali…

1386
02:44:29,093 --> 02:44:31,552
God is watching everything.

1387
02:44:31,760 --> 02:44:35,552
He will definitely punish you.

1388
02:44:58,427 --> 02:45:01,093
You can't even look directly at the sun.

1389
02:45:01,427 --> 02:45:04,093
How dare you speak ill of the God
whose vision is as wide spread?

1390
02:45:04,677 --> 02:45:06,843
You can't even touch fire.

1391
02:45:07,135 --> 02:45:09,802
How dare you seek to destroy
the God whose eyes are fire?

1392
02:45:10,260 --> 02:45:13,260
You are but a scavenging dog
searching for scraps in the desert.

1393
02:45:13,593 --> 02:45:16,968
And you dare challenge the Lord
who sustains the infinite universe?

1394
02:45:17,468 --> 02:45:20,260
Hey! We are Hindus.

1395
02:45:20,468 --> 02:45:23,927
Righteousness is our way of life.
Compassion is our nature.

1396
02:45:24,218 --> 02:45:26,760
We shelter anyone who seeks refuge.

1397
02:45:26,927 --> 02:45:29,427
We help anyone who asks for aid.

1398
02:45:29,677 --> 02:45:33,260
But if you mistake that kindness
for weakness and raise your sword…

1399
02:45:33,385 --> 02:45:37,218
we will turn your heads into skulls
and wear them around our necks.

1400
02:45:37,427 --> 02:45:39,509
This alone is eternal!

1401
02:45:39,510 --> 02:45:42,552
Hara Hara Mahadev!

1402
02:45:42,885 --> 02:45:46,177
Hara Hara Mahadev!

1403
02:45:58,093 --> 02:46:01,010
So… what lies behind that door, Aunt?

1404
02:46:01,302 --> 02:46:04,927
To know that, we must know what transpired

1405
02:46:05,218 --> 02:46:09,218
between the end of the Dwapara Yuga
and the dawn of the Kali Yuga.

